#. type: Yaml Front Matter Hash Value: description
#, no-wrap
msgid "A free IBM course on quantum information and computation"
msgstr "Isang libreng kursong IBM sa quantum information at computation"

#. type: Yaml Front Matter Hash Value: sidebar_label
#, no-wrap
msgid "Stabilizer codes"
msgstr "Mga stabilizer code"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"{/* cspell:ignore notin */}\n"
"{/* cspell:ignore operatorname */}\n"
msgstr ""
"{/* cspell:ignore notin */}\n"
"{/* cspell:ignore operatorname */}\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Now we'll define stabilizer codes in general.\n"
"We'll also discuss some of their basic properties and how they work, including how states can be encoded and how errors are detected and corrected using these codes.\n"
msgstr ""
"Ngayon ay tukuyin natin ang mga stabilizer code sa pangkalahatan.\n"
"Tatalakayin din natin ang ilan sa kanilang mga pangunahing katangian at kung paano sila gumagana, kasama na kung paano ma-encode ang mga estado at kung paano natutuklas at naitatama ang mga error gamit ang mga code na ito.\n"

#. type: Title ##
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Definition of stabilizer codes {#definition-of-stabilizer-codes}"
msgstr "Kahulugan ng mga stabilizer code {#definition-of-stabilizer-codes}"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"An $n$-qubit stabilizer code is specified by a list of $n$-qubit Pauli operations, $P_1,\\ldots,P_r.$\n"
"These operations are called *stabilizer generators* in this context, and they must satisfy the following three properties.\n"
msgstr ""
"Ang isang $n$-qubit stabilizer code ay tinutukoy ng isang listahan ng $n$-qubit na mga Pauli operation, $P_1,\\ldots,P_r.$\n"
"Ang mga operation na ito ay tinatawag na *mga stabilizer generator* sa kontekstong ito, at dapat nilang matugunan ang sumusunod na tatlong katangian.\n"

#. type: Bullet: '1. '
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "The stabilizer generators all *commute* with one another.\n"
msgstr "Ang lahat ng stabilizer generator ay *commute* sa isa't isa.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"   $$\n"
"   P_j P_k = P_k P_j \\qquad \\text{(for all $j,k\\in\\{1,\\ldots,r\\}$)}\n"
"   $$\n"
msgstr ""
"   $$\n"
"   P_j P_k = P_k P_j \\qquad \\text{(para sa lahat ng $j,k\\in\\{1,\\ldots,r\\}$)}\n"
"   $$\n"

#. type: Bullet: '2. '
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "The stabilizer generators form a *minimal generating set*.\n"
msgstr ""
"Ang mga stabilizer generator ay bumubuo ng isang *minimal generating set*.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"   $$\n"
"   P_k \\notin \\langle P_1,\\ldots,P_{k-1},P_{k+1},\\ldots,P_r\\rangle \\qquad \\text{(for all $k\\in\\{1,\\ldots,r\\}$)}\n"
"   $$\n"
msgstr ""
"   $$\n"
"   P_k \\notin \\langle P_1,\\ldots,P_{k-1},P_{k+1},\\ldots,P_r\\rangle \\qquad \\text{(para sa lahat ng $k\\in\\{1,\\ldots,r\\}$)}\n"
"   $$\n"

#. type: Bullet: '3. '
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"At least one quantum state vector is fixed by all of the stabilizer "
"generators.\n"
msgstr ""
"May hindi bababa sa isang quantum state vector na naayos ng lahat ng "
"stabilizer generator.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"   $$\n"
"   -\\mathbb{I}^{\\otimes n} \\notin \\langle P_1,\\ldots, P_r\\rangle\n"
"   $$\n"
msgstr ""
"   $$\n"
"   -\\mathbb{I}^{\\otimes n} \\notin \\langle P_1,\\ldots, P_r\\rangle\n"
"   $$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"   (It's not obvious that the existence of a quantum state vector "
"$\\vert\\psi\\rangle$ fixed by all of the stabilizer generators, meaning "
"$P_1 \\vert\\psi\\rangle = \\cdots = P_r \\vert\\psi\\rangle = "
"\\vert\\psi\\rangle,$ is equivalent to $-\\mathbb{I}^{\\otimes n} \\notin "
"\\langle P_1,\\ldots, P_r\\rangle,$ but indeed this is the case, and we'll "
"see why a bit later in the lesson.)\n"
msgstr ""
"   (Hindi agad malinaw na ang pag-iral ng isang quantum state vector na "
"$\\vert\\psi\\rangle$ na naayos ng lahat ng stabilizer generator, ibig "
"sabihin $P_1 \\vert\\psi\\rangle = \\cdots = P_r \\vert\\psi\\rangle = "
"\\vert\\psi\\rangle,$ ay katumbas ng $-\\mathbb{I}^{\\otimes n} \\notin "
"\\langle P_1,\\ldots, P_r\\rangle,$ ngunit totoong ganito ang kaso, at "
"makikita natin kung bakit sa bandang huli ng aralin.)\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Assuming that we have such a list $P_1,\\ldots,P_r,$ the *code space* "
"defined by these stabilizer generators is the subspace $\\mathcal{C}$ "
"containing every $n$-qubit quantum state vector fixed by all $r$ of these "
"stabilizer generators.\n"
msgstr ""
"Kung mayroon tayong ganoong listahan na $P_1,\\ldots,P_r,$ ang *code space* "
"na tinukoy ng mga stabilizer generator na ito ay ang subspace na "
"$\\mathcal{C}$ na naglalaman ng bawat $n$-qubit quantum state vector na "
"naayos ng lahat ng $r$ na stabilizer generator na ito.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"\\mathcal{C} = \\bigl\\{ \\vert\\psi\\rangle \\,:\\, P_1 \\vert\\psi\\rangle = \\cdots = P_r \\vert\\psi\\rangle = \\vert\\psi\\rangle \\bigr\\}\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"\\mathcal{C} = \\bigl\\{ \\vert\\psi\\rangle \\,:\\, P_1 \\vert\\psi\\rangle = \\cdots = P_r \\vert\\psi\\rangle = \\vert\\psi\\rangle \\bigr\\}\n"
"$$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Quantum state vectors in this subspace are precisely the ones that can be viewed as *valid encodings* of quantum states.\n"
"We'll discuss the actual process of encoding later.\n"
msgstr ""
"Ang mga quantum state vector sa subspace na ito ay eksakto ang mga maaaring ituring bilang *mga wastong encoding* ng mga quantum estado.\n"
"Tatalakayin natin ang aktwal na proseso ng pag-encode sa bandang huli.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Finally, the *stabilizer* of the code defined by the stabilizer generators "
"$P_1, \\ldots, P_r$ is the set generated by these operations:\n"
msgstr ""
"Sa wakas, ang *stabilizer* ng code na tinukoy ng mga stabilizer generator na"
" $P_1, \\ldots, P_r$ ay ang set na binuo ng mga operation na ito:\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"\\langle P_1,\\ldots,P_r\\rangle.\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"\\langle P_1,\\ldots,P_r\\rangle.\n"
"$$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"A natural way to think about a stabilizer code is to view the stabilizer generators as observables, and to collectively interpret the outcomes of the measurements associated with these observables as an error syndrome.\n"
"Valid encodings are $n$-qubit quantum state vectors for which the measurement outcomes, as eigenvalues, are all guaranteed to be $+1.$\n"
"Any other syndrome, where at least one $-1$ measurement outcome occurs, signals that an error has been detected.\n"
msgstr ""
"Ang natural na paraan upang isipin ang isang stabilizer code ay ang tingnan ang mga stabilizer generator bilang mga observable, at kolektibong bigyang-kahulugan ang mga resulta ng mga sukat na nauugnay sa mga observable na ito bilang isang error syndrome.\n"
"Ang mga wastong encoding ay $n$-qubit quantum state vector kung saan ang mga resulta ng sukat, bilang mga eigenvalue, ay garantisadong $+1$ lahat.\n"
"Ang anumang iba pang syndrome, kung saan may kahit isang $-1$ na resulta ng sukat, ay nagpapahiwatig na natuklas ang isang error.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"We'll take a look at several examples shortly, but first just a few remarks "
"about the three conditions on stabilizer generators are in order.\n"
msgstr ""
"Titingnan natin ang ilang halimbawa sa lalong madaling panahon, ngunit una "
"ay ilang komento tungkol sa tatlong kondisyon sa mga stabilizer generator "
"ang nararapat.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"The first condition is natural, in light of the interpretation of the stabilizer generators as observables, for it implies that it doesn't matter in what order the measurements are performed: the observables commute, so the measurements commute.\n"
"This naturally imposes certain algebraic constraints on stabilizer codes that are important to how they work.\n"
msgstr ""
"Ang unang kondisyon ay natural, sa liwanag ng interpretasyon ng mga stabilizer generator bilang mga observable, dahil ipinahihiwatig nito na hindi mahalaga kung sa anong pagkakasunod-sunod ginaganap ang mga sukat: ang mga observable ay commute, kaya ang mga sukat ay commute rin.\n"
"Ang ito ay natural na nagpapataw ng ilang algebraic na hadlang sa mga stabilizer code na mahalaga sa kung paano sila gumagana.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"The second condition requires that the stabilizer generators form a minimal generating set, meaning that removing any one of them would result in a smaller stabilizer.\n"
"Strictly speaking, this condition isn't really essential to the way stabilizer codes work in an *operational* sense — and, as we'll see in the next lesson, it does sometimes make sense to think about sets of stabilizer generators for codes that actually don't satisfy this condition.\n"
"For the sake of *analyzing* stabilizer codes and explaining their properties, however, we will assume that this condition is in place.\n"
"In short, this condition guarantees that each observable that we measure to obtain the error syndrome *adds* information about possible errors, as opposed to being redundant and producing results that could be inferred from the other stabilizer generator measurements.\n"
msgstr ""
"Ang pangalawang kondisyon ay nangangailangan na ang mga stabilizer generator ay bumubuo ng isang minimal generating set, ibig sabihin, ang pag-aalis ng kahit isa sa kanila ay magreresulta sa isang mas maliit na stabilizer.\n"
"Sa mahigpit na pagsasalita, ang kondisyong ito ay hindi talagang mahalaga sa paraan ng paggana ng mga stabilizer code sa isang *operasyonal* na kahulugan — at, tulad ng makikita natin sa susunod na aralin, minsan ay may saysay na pag-isipan ang mga set ng stabilizer generator para sa mga code na hindi aktwal na natutugunan ang kondisyong ito.\n"
"Para sa kapakanan ng *pagsusuri* ng mga stabilizer code at pagpapaliwanag ng kanilang mga katangian, gayunpaman, ipagpapalagay natin na ang kondisyong ito ay nasa lugar.\n"
"Sa madaling salita, tinitiyak ng kondisyong ito na ang bawat observable na sinusukat natin upang makuha ang error syndrome ay nagdadagdag ng impormasyon tungkol sa mga posibleng error, sa halip na maging redundante at gumagawa ng mga resulta na maaaring mahiwatig mula sa iba pang mga sukat ng stabilizer generator.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"The third condition requires that at least one nonzero vector is fixed by all of the stabilizer generators, which is equivalent to $-\\mathbb{I}^{\\otimes n}$ not being contained in the stabilizer.\n"
"The need for this condition comes from the fact that it actually is possible to choose a minimal generating set of $n$-qubit Pauli operations that all commute with one another, and yet no nonzero vectors are fixed by every one of the operations.\n"
"We're not interested in \"codes\" for which there are no valid encodings, so we rule out this possibility by requiring this condition as a part of the definition.\n"
msgstr ""
"Ang ikatlong kondisyon ay nangangailangan na hindi bababa sa isang nonzero na vector ay naayos ng lahat ng stabilizer generator, na katumbas ng $-\\mathbb{I}^{\\otimes n}$ na hindi nakapaloob sa stabilizer.\n"
"Ang pangangailangan para sa kondisyong ito ay nagmumula sa katotohanang posible talaga ang pumili ng isang minimal generating set ng $n$-qubit na mga Pauli operation na lahat ay commute sa isa't isa, gayunpaman walang nonzero na vector ang naayos ng bawat isa sa mga operation.\n"
"Hindi tayo interesado sa mga \"code\" na walang wastong encoding, kaya itinatanggal natin ang posibilidad na ito sa pamamagitan ng pag-aatas ng kondisyong ito bilang bahagi ng kahulugan.\n"

#. type: Title ##
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Examples {#examples}"
msgstr "Mga halimbawa {#examples}"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Here are some examples of stabilizer codes for small values of $n.$\n"
"We'll see more examples, including ones for which $n$ can be much larger, in the next lesson.\n"
msgstr ""
"Narito ang ilang halimbawa ng mga stabilizer code para sa maliliit na halaga ng $n.$\n"
"Makikita natin ang higit pang mga halimbawa, kasama na ang mga kung saan ang $n$ ay maaaring mas malaki, sa susunod na aralin.\n"

#. type: Title ###
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "3-bit repetition code {#3-bit-repetition-code}"
msgstr "3-bit repetition code {#3-bit-repetition-code}"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"The 3-bit repetition code is an example of a stabilizer code, where our stabilizer generators are\n"
"$Z \\otimes Z \\otimes \\mathbb{I}$ and $\\mathbb{I} \\otimes Z \\otimes Z.$\n"
msgstr ""
"Ang 3-bit repetition code ay isang halimbawa ng isang stabilizer code, kung saan ang ating mga stabilizer generator ay\n"
"$Z \\otimes Z \\otimes \\mathbb{I}$ at $\\mathbb{I} \\otimes Z \\otimes Z.$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"We can easily check that these two stabilizer generators fulfill the required conditions.\n"
"First, the two stabilizer generators $Z \\otimes Z \\otimes \\mathbb{I}$ and $\\mathbb{I} \\otimes Z \\otimes Z$ commute with one another.\n"
msgstr ""
"Madali nating masusuri na ang dalawang stabilizer generator na ito ay natutugunan ang mga kinakailangang kondisyon.\n"
"Una, ang dalawang stabilizer generator na $Z \\otimes Z \\otimes \\mathbb{I}$ at $\\mathbb{I} \\otimes Z \\otimes Z$ ay commute sa isa't isa.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"(Z \\otimes Z \\otimes \\mathbb{I})(\\mathbb{I} \\otimes Z \\otimes Z) = Z \\otimes \\mathbb{I} \\otimes Z\n"
"= (\\mathbb{I} \\otimes Z \\otimes Z)(Z \\otimes Z \\otimes \\mathbb{I})\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"(Z \\otimes Z \\otimes \\mathbb{I})(\\mathbb{I} \\otimes Z \\otimes Z) = Z \\otimes \\mathbb{I} \\otimes Z\n"
"= (\\mathbb{I} \\otimes Z \\otimes Z)(Z \\otimes Z \\otimes \\mathbb{I})\n"
"$$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Second, we have a minimal generating set (rather trivially in this case).\n"
msgstr ""
"Pangalawa, mayroon tayong minimal generating set (medyo maliwanag sa kasong "
"ito).\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"\\begin{aligned}\n"
"Z \\otimes Z \\otimes \\mathbb{I} \\notin \\langle\\mathbb{I} \\otimes Z \\otimes Z\\rangle\n"
"& = \\{\\mathbb{I}\\otimes\\mathbb{I}\\otimes\\mathbb{I}, \\mathbb{I} \\otimes Z \\otimes Z\\}\\\\[1mm]\n"
"\\mathbb{I} \\otimes Z \\otimes Z \\notin \\langle Z \\otimes Z \\otimes \\mathbb{I}\\rangle\n"
"& = \\{\\mathbb{I}\\otimes\\mathbb{I}\\otimes\\mathbb{I}, Z \\otimes Z \\otimes \\mathbb{I}\\}\n"
"\\end{aligned}\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"\\begin{aligned}\n"
"Z \\otimes Z \\otimes \\mathbb{I} \\notin \\langle\\mathbb{I} \\otimes Z \\otimes Z\\rangle\n"
"& = \\{\\mathbb{I}\\otimes\\mathbb{I}\\otimes\\mathbb{I}, \\mathbb{I} \\otimes Z \\otimes Z\\}\\\\[1mm]\n"
"\\mathbb{I} \\otimes Z \\otimes Z \\notin \\langle Z \\otimes Z \\otimes \\mathbb{I}\\rangle\n"
"& = \\{\\mathbb{I}\\otimes\\mathbb{I}\\otimes\\mathbb{I}, Z \\otimes Z \\otimes \\mathbb{I}\\}\n"
"\\end{aligned}\n"
"$$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"And third, we already know that $\\vert 000\\rangle$ and $\\vert 111\\rangle,$ as well as any linear combination of these vectors, are fixed by both $Z \\otimes Z \\otimes \\mathbb{I}$ and $\\mathbb{I} \\otimes Z \\otimes Z.$\n"
"Alternatively, we can conclude this using the equivalent condition from the definition.\n"
msgstr ""
"At pangatlo, alam na natin na ang $\\vert 000\\rangle$ at $\\vert 111\\rangle,$ pati na rin ang anumang linear na kombinasyon ng mga vector na ito, ay naayos ng parehong $Z \\otimes Z \\otimes \\mathbb{I}$ at $\\mathbb{I} \\otimes Z \\otimes Z.$\n"
"Bilang alternatibo, maaari nating tapusin ito gamit ang katumbas na kondisyon mula sa kahulugan.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"-\\mathbb{I}\\otimes\\mathbb{I}\\otimes\\mathbb{I}\\notin\n"
"\\langle Z \\otimes Z \\otimes \\mathbb{I}, \\mathbb{I} \\otimes Z \\otimes Z\\rangle\n"
"= \\{\n"
"  \\mathbb{I}\\otimes\\mathbb{I}\\otimes\\mathbb{I},\n"
"  Z\\otimes Z\\otimes\\mathbb{I},\n"
"  Z\\otimes\\mathbb{I}\\otimes Z,\n"
"  \\mathbb{I}\\otimes Z\\otimes Z\n"
"\\}\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"-\\mathbb{I}\\otimes\\mathbb{I}\\otimes\\mathbb{I}\\notin\n"
"\\langle Z \\otimes Z \\otimes \\mathbb{I}, \\mathbb{I} \\otimes Z \\otimes Z\\rangle\n"
"= \\{\n"
"  \\mathbb{I}\\otimes\\mathbb{I}\\otimes\\mathbb{I},\n"
"  Z\\otimes Z\\otimes\\mathbb{I},\n"
"  Z\\otimes\\mathbb{I}\\otimes Z,\n"
"  \\mathbb{I}\\otimes Z\\otimes Z\n"
"\\}\n"
"$$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"These conditions can be much more difficult to check for more complicated "
"stabilizer codes.\n"
msgstr ""
"Ang mga kondisyong ito ay maaaring maging mas mahirap suriin para sa mas "
"kumplikadong mga stabilizer code.\n"

#. type: Title ###
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Modified 3-bit repetition code {#modified-3-bit-repetition-code}"
msgstr "Binagong 3-bit repetition code {#modified-3-bit-repetition-code}"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"In the previous lesson, we saw that it's possible to modify the 3-bit repetition code so that it protects against phase-flip errors rather than bit-flip errors.\n"
"As a stabilizer code, this new code is easy to describe:\n"
"its stabilizer generators are $X \\otimes X \\otimes \\mathbb{I}$ and $\\mathbb{I} \\otimes X \\otimes X.$\n"
msgstr ""
"Sa nakaraang aralin, nakita natin na posible ang baguhin ang 3-bit repetition code upang maprotektahan laban sa mga phase-flip error sa halip na mga bit-flip error.\n"
"Bilang isang stabilizer code, ang bagong code na ito ay madaling ilarawan:\n"
"ang mga stabilizer generator nito ay $X \\otimes X \\otimes \\mathbb{I}$ at $\\mathbb{I} \\otimes X \\otimes X.$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"This time the stabilizer generators represent $X\\otimes X$ observables rather than $Z\\otimes Z$ observables, so they're essentially parity checks in the plus/minus basis rather than the standard basis.\n"
"The three required conditions on the stabilizer generators are easily verified, along similar lines to the ordinary 3-bit repetition code.\n"
msgstr ""
"Sa pagkakataong ito ang mga stabilizer generator ay kumakatawan sa mga $X\\otimes X$ observable sa halip na mga $Z\\otimes Z$ observable, kaya sila ay mahalagang mga parity check sa plus/minus basis sa halip na sa standard basis.\n"
"Ang tatlong kinakailangang kondisyon sa mga stabilizer generator ay madaling mapatunayan, sa katulad na paraan tulad ng sa ordinaryong 3-bit repetition code.\n"

#. type: Title ###
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "9-qubit Shor code {#9-qubit-shor-code}"
msgstr "9-qubit Shor code {#9-qubit-shor-code}"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Here's the 9-qubit Shor code, which is also a stabilizer code, expressed by "
"stabilizer generators.\n"
msgstr ""
"Narito ang 9-qubit Shor code, na isa ring stabilizer code, na ipinahahayag "
"ng mga stabilizer generator.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"\\begin{gathered}\n"
"Z \\otimes Z \\otimes \\mathbb{I} \\otimes\n"
"\\mathbb{I} \\otimes \\mathbb{I} \\otimes \\mathbb{I} \\otimes\n"
"\\mathbb{I} \\otimes \\mathbb{I} \\otimes \\mathbb{I}\\\\[1mm]\n"
"\\mathbb{I} \\otimes Z \\otimes Z \\otimes\n"
"\\mathbb{I} \\otimes \\mathbb{I} \\otimes \\mathbb{I} \\otimes\n"
"\\mathbb{I} \\otimes \\mathbb{I} \\otimes \\mathbb{I}\\\\[1mm]\n"
"\\mathbb{I} \\otimes \\mathbb{I} \\otimes \\mathbb{I} \\otimes\n"
"Z \\otimes Z \\otimes \\mathbb{I} \\otimes\n"
"\\mathbb{I} \\otimes \\mathbb{I} \\otimes \\mathbb{I}\\\\[1mm]\n"
"\\mathbb{I} \\otimes \\mathbb{I} \\otimes \\mathbb{I} \\otimes\n"
"\\mathbb{I} \\otimes Z \\otimes Z \\otimes\n"
"\\mathbb{I} \\otimes \\mathbb{I} \\otimes \\mathbb{I}\\\\[1mm]\n"
"\\mathbb{I} \\otimes \\mathbb{I} \\otimes \\mathbb{I} \\otimes\n"
"\\mathbb{I} \\otimes \\mathbb{I} \\otimes \\mathbb{I} \\otimes\n"
"Z \\otimes Z \\otimes \\mathbb{I}\\\\[1mm]\n"
"\\mathbb{I} \\otimes \\mathbb{I} \\otimes \\mathbb{I} \\otimes\n"
"\\mathbb{I} \\otimes \\mathbb{I} \\otimes \\mathbb{I} \\otimes\n"
"\\mathbb{I} \\otimes Z \\otimes Z\\\\[1mm]\n"
"X \\otimes X \\otimes X \\otimes X \\otimes X \\otimes X \\otimes\n"
"\\mathbb{I} \\otimes \\mathbb{I} \\otimes \\mathbb{I}\\\\[1mm]\n"
"\\mathbb{I} \\otimes \\mathbb{I} \\otimes \\mathbb{I}\\otimes\n"
"X \\otimes X \\otimes X \\otimes X \\otimes X \\otimes X\n"
"\\end{gathered}\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"\\begin{gathered}\n"
"Z \\otimes Z \\otimes \\mathbb{I} \\otimes\n"
"\\mathbb{I} \\otimes \\mathbb{I} \\otimes \\mathbb{I} \\otimes\n"
"\\mathbb{I} \\otimes \\mathbb{I} \\otimes \\mathbb{I}\\\\[1mm]\n"
"\\mathbb{I} \\otimes Z \\otimes Z \\otimes\n"
"\\mathbb{I} \\otimes \\mathbb{I} \\otimes \\mathbb{I} \\otimes\n"
"\\mathbb{I} \\otimes \\mathbb{I} \\otimes \\mathbb{I}\\\\[1mm]\n"
"\\mathbb{I} \\otimes \\mathbb{I} \\otimes \\mathbb{I} \\otimes\n"
"Z \\otimes Z \\otimes \\mathbb{I} \\otimes\n"
"\\mathbb{I} \\otimes \\mathbb{I} \\otimes \\mathbb{I}\\\\[1mm]\n"
"\\mathbb{I} \\otimes \\mathbb{I} \\otimes \\mathbb{I} \\otimes\n"
"\\mathbb{I} \\otimes Z \\otimes Z \\otimes\n"
"\\mathbb{I} \\otimes \\mathbb{I} \\otimes \\mathbb{I}\\\\[1mm]\n"
"\\mathbb{I} \\otimes \\mathbb{I} \\otimes \\mathbb{I} \\otimes\n"
"\\mathbb{I} \\otimes \\mathbb{I} \\otimes \\mathbb{I} \\otimes\n"
"Z \\otimes Z \\otimes \\mathbb{I}\\\\[1mm]\n"
"\\mathbb{I} \\otimes \\mathbb{I} \\otimes \\mathbb{I} \\otimes\n"
"\\mathbb{I} \\otimes \\mathbb{I} \\otimes \\mathbb{I} \\otimes\n"
"\\mathbb{I} \\otimes Z \\otimes Z\\\\[1mm]\n"
"X \\otimes X \\otimes X \\otimes X \\otimes X \\otimes X \\otimes\n"
"\\mathbb{I} \\otimes \\mathbb{I} \\otimes \\mathbb{I}\\\\[1mm]\n"
"\\mathbb{I} \\otimes \\mathbb{I} \\otimes \\mathbb{I}\\otimes\n"
"X \\otimes X \\otimes X \\otimes X \\otimes X \\otimes X\n"
"\\end{gathered}\n"
"$$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"In this case, we basically have three copies of the 3-bit repetition code, one for each of the three blocks of three qubits,\n"
"as well as the last two stabilizer generators, which take a form reminiscent of the circuit for detecting phase flips for this code.\n"
msgstr ""
"Sa kasong ito, mayroon tayong tatlong kopya ng 3-bit repetition code, isa para sa bawat isa sa tatlong bloke ng tatlong qubit,\n"
"pati na rin ang huling dalawang stabilizer generator, na may hugis na kapareho ng Circuit para sa pag-detect ng mga phase flip para sa code na ito.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"An alternative way to think about the last two stabilizer generators is that"
" they take the same form as for the 3-bit repetition code for phase flips, "
"except that $X\\otimes X\\otimes X$ is substituted for $X,$ which is "
"consistent with the fact that $X\\otimes X\\otimes X$ corresponds to an $X$ "
"operation on logical qubits encoded using the 3-bit repetition code.\n"
msgstr ""
"Ang alternatibong paraan upang pag-isipan ang huling dalawang stabilizer "
"generator ay na sila ay may parehong hugis tulad ng para sa 3-bit repetition"
" code para sa mga phase flip, maliban na ang $X\\otimes X\\otimes X$ ay "
"kapalit ng $X,$ na naaayon sa katotohanang ang $X\\otimes X\\otimes X$ ay "
"tumutugma sa isang $X$ na operation sa mga logical qubit na na-encode gamit "
"ang 3-bit repetition code.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Before we move on to other examples, it should be noted that tensor product symbols are often omitted when describing stabilizer codes by lists of stabilizer generators, because it tends to make them easier to read and to see their patterns.\n"
"For example, the same stabilizer generators as above for the 9-qubit Shor code look like this without the tensor product symbols being written explicitly.\n"
msgstr ""
"Bago tayo lumipat sa iba pang mga halimbawa, dapat tandaan na ang mga tensor product symbol ay madalas na inalis kapag inilalarawan ang mga stabilizer code sa pamamagitan ng mga listahan ng stabilizer generator, dahil ito ay karaniwang nagpapagaan ng pagbabasa at pagkita ng kanilang mga pattern.\n"
"Halimbawa, ang mga parehong stabilizer generator tulad ng nasa itaas para sa 9-qubit Shor code ay ganito ang hitsura nang hindi isinusulat nang malinaw ang mga tensor product symbol.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"\\begin{array}{ccccccccc}\n"
"Z & Z & \\mathbb{I} &\n"
"\\mathbb{I} & \\mathbb{I} & \\mathbb{I} &\n"
"\\mathbb{I} & \\mathbb{I} & \\mathbb{I}\\\\[1mm]\n"
"\\mathbb{I} & Z & Z &\n"
"\\mathbb{I} & \\mathbb{I} & \\mathbb{I} &\n"
"\\mathbb{I} & \\mathbb{I} & \\mathbb{I}\\\\[1mm]\n"
"\\mathbb{I} & \\mathbb{I} & \\mathbb{I} &\n"
"Z & Z & \\mathbb{I} &\n"
"\\mathbb{I} & \\mathbb{I} & \\mathbb{I}\\\\[1mm]\n"
"\\mathbb{I} & \\mathbb{I} & \\mathbb{I} &\n"
"\\mathbb{I} & Z & Z &\n"
"\\mathbb{I} & \\mathbb{I} & \\mathbb{I}\\\\[1mm]\n"
"\\mathbb{I} & \\mathbb{I} & \\mathbb{I} &\n"
"\\mathbb{I} & \\mathbb{I} & \\mathbb{I} &\n"
"Z & Z & \\mathbb{I}\\\\[1mm]\n"
"\\mathbb{I} & \\mathbb{I} & \\mathbb{I} &\n"
"\\mathbb{I} & \\mathbb{I} & \\mathbb{I} &\n"
"\\mathbb{I} & Z & Z\\\\[1mm]\n"
"X & X & X & X & X & X &\n"
"\\mathbb{I} & \\mathbb{I} & \\mathbb{I}\\\\[1mm]\n"
"\\mathbb{I} & \\mathbb{I} & \\mathbb{I}&\n"
"X & X & X & X & X & X\n"
"\\end{array}\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"\\begin{array}{ccccccccc}\n"
"Z & Z & \\mathbb{I} &\n"
"\\mathbb{I} & \\mathbb{I} & \\mathbb{I} &\n"
"\\mathbb{I} & \\mathbb{I} & \\mathbb{I}\\\\[1mm]\n"
"\\mathbb{I} & Z & Z &\n"
"\\mathbb{I} & \\mathbb{I} & \\mathbb{I} &\n"
"\\mathbb{I} & \\mathbb{I} & \\mathbb{I}\\\\[1mm]\n"
"\\mathbb{I} & \\mathbb{I} & \\mathbb{I} &\n"
"Z & Z & \\mathbb{I} &\n"
"\\mathbb{I} & \\mathbb{I} & \\mathbb{I}\\\\[1mm]\n"
"\\mathbb{I} & \\mathbb{I} & \\mathbb{I} &\n"
"\\mathbb{I} & Z & Z &\n"
"\\mathbb{I} & \\mathbb{I} & \\mathbb{I}\\\\[1mm]\n"
"\\mathbb{I} & \\mathbb{I} & \\mathbb{I} &\n"
"\\mathbb{I} & \\mathbb{I} & \\mathbb{I} &\n"
"Z & Z & \\mathbb{I}\\\\[1mm]\n"
"\\mathbb{I} & \\mathbb{I} & \\mathbb{I} &\n"
"\\mathbb{I} & \\mathbb{I} & \\mathbb{I} &\n"
"\\mathbb{I} & Z & Z\\\\[1mm]\n"
"X & X & X & X & X & X &\n"
"\\mathbb{I} & \\mathbb{I} & \\mathbb{I}\\\\[1mm]\n"
"\\mathbb{I} & \\mathbb{I} & \\mathbb{I}&\n"
"X & X & X & X & X & X\n"
"\\end{array}\n"
"$$\n"

#. type: Title ###
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "7-qubit Steane code {#7-qubit-steane-code}"
msgstr "7-qubit Steane code {#7-qubit-steane-code}"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Here's another example of a stabilizer code, known as the *7-qubit Steane code*.\n"
"It has some remarkable features, and we'll come back to this code from time to time throughout the remaining lessons of the course.\n"
msgstr ""
"Narito ang isa pang halimbawa ng isang stabilizer code, na kilala bilang *7-qubit Steane code*.\n"
"Mayroon itong ilang kapansin-pansing katangian, at babalik tayo sa code na ito paminsan-minsan sa natitirang mga aralin ng kurso.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"\\begin{array}{ccccccc}\n"
"Z & Z & Z & Z & \\mathbb{I} & \\mathbb{I} & \\mathbb{I} \\\\[1mm]\n"
"Z & Z & \\mathbb{I} & \\mathbb{I} & Z & Z & \\mathbb{I} \\\\[1mm]\n"
"Z & \\mathbb{I} & Z & \\mathbb{I} & Z & \\mathbb{I} & Z \\\\[1mm]\n"
"X & X & X & X & \\mathbb{I} & \\mathbb{I} & \\mathbb{I} \\\\[1mm]\n"
"X & X & \\mathbb{I} & \\mathbb{I} & X & X & \\mathbb{I} \\\\[1mm]\n"
"X & \\mathbb{I} & X & \\mathbb{I} & X & \\mathbb{I} & X\n"
"\\end{array}\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"\\begin{array}{ccccccc}\n"
"Z & Z & Z & Z & \\mathbb{I} & \\mathbb{I} & \\mathbb{I} \\\\[1mm]\n"
"Z & Z & \\mathbb{I} & \\mathbb{I} & Z & Z & \\mathbb{I} \\\\[1mm]\n"
"Z & \\mathbb{I} & Z & \\mathbb{I} & Z & \\mathbb{I} & Z \\\\[1mm]\n"
"X & X & X & X & \\mathbb{I} & \\mathbb{I} & \\mathbb{I} \\\\[1mm]\n"
"X & X & \\mathbb{I} & \\mathbb{I} & X & X & \\mathbb{I} \\\\[1mm]\n"
"X & \\mathbb{I} & X & \\mathbb{I} & X & \\mathbb{I} & X\n"
"\\end{array}\n"
"$$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"For now, let's simply observe that this is a valid stabilizer code.\n"
"The first three stabilizer generators clearly commute with one another, because $Z$ commutes with itself and the identity commutes with everything, and the situation is similar for the last three stabilizer generators.\n"
"It remains to check that if we take one of the $Z$-stabilizer generators (that is, one of the first three) and one of the $X$-stabilizer generators (that is, one of the last three), then these two generators commute, and one can go through the 9 possible pairings to check that.\n"
"In all of these cases, an $X$ and a $Z$ Pauli matrix always line up in the same position an even number of times, so the two generators will commute, just like $X\\otimes X$ and $Z\\otimes Z$ commute.\n"
"This is also a minimal generating set, and it defines a nontrivial code space, which are facts left to you to contemplate.\n"
msgstr ""
"Sa ngayon, obserbahan lamang natin na ito ay isang wastong stabilizer code.\n"
"Malinaw na nag-commute ang unang tatlong stabilizer generator sa isa't isa, dahil ang $Z$ ay nag-commute sa sarili nito at ang identity ay nag-commute sa lahat, at katulad ang sitwasyon para sa huling tatlong stabilizer generator.\n"
"Nananatili pang suriin na kung kukuha tayo ng isa sa mga $Z$-stabilizer generator (ibig sabihin, isa sa mga unang tatlo) at isa sa mga $X$-stabilizer generator (ibig sabihin, isa sa mga huling tatlo), ang dalawang generator na ito ay nag-commute, at maaaring suriin ang 9 na posibleng pares upang patunayan iyon.\n"
"Sa lahat ng kasong ito, ang isang $X$ at isang $Z$ na Pauli matrix ay palaging nakahanay sa parehong posisyon nang pantay na bilang ng beses, kaya ang dalawang generator ay mag-co-commute, tulad ng $X\\otimes X$ at $Z\\otimes Z$ na nag-commute.\n"
"Ito rin ay isang minimal generating set, at nagtatakda ito ng isang nontrivial na code space, na mga katotohanang iniiwan sa inyo upang pag-isipan.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"The 7-qubit Steane code is similar to the 9-qubit Shor code in that it "
"encodes a single qubit and allows for the correction of an arbitrary error "
"on one qubit, but it requires only 7 qubits rather than 9.\n"
msgstr ""
"Ang 7-qubit Steane code ay katulad ng 9-qubit Shor code sa na ini-encode "
"nito ang isang solong qubit at nagpapahintulot ng pagwawasto ng isang "
"arbitrary na error sa isang qubit, ngunit nangangailangan lamang ito ng 7 "
"qubit sa halip na 9.\n"

#. type: Title ###
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "5-qubit code {#5-qubit-code}"
msgstr "5-qubit code {#5-qubit-code}"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Seven is not the fewest number of qubits required to encode one qubit and "
"protect it against an arbitrary error on one qubit — here's a stabilizer "
"code that does this using just 5 qubits.\n"
msgstr ""
"Pitong ay hindi ang pinakamaliit na bilang ng mga qubit na kinakailangan "
"upang mag-encode ng isang qubit at maprotektahan ito laban sa isang "
"arbitrary na error sa isang qubit — narito ang isang stabilizer code na "
"ginagawa ito gamit lamang ang 5 qubit.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"\\begin{array}{ccccc}\n"
"X & Z & Z & X & \\mathbb{I} \\\\[1mm]\n"
"\\mathbb{I} & X & Z & Z & X \\\\[1mm]\n"
"X & \\mathbb{I} & X & Z & Z \\\\[1mm]\n"
"Z & X & \\mathbb{I} & X & Z \\\\[1mm]\n"
"\\end{array}\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"\\begin{array}{ccccc}\n"
"X & Z & Z & X & \\mathbb{I} \\\\[1mm]\n"
"\\mathbb{I} & X & Z & Z & X \\\\[1mm]\n"
"X & \\mathbb{I} & X & Z & Z \\\\[1mm]\n"
"Z & X & \\mathbb{I} & X & Z \\\\[1mm]\n"
"\\end{array}\n"
"$$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"This code is typically called *the 5-qubit code.*\n"
"This is the smallest number of qubits in a quantum error correcting code that can allow for the correction of an arbitrary single-qubit error.\n"
msgstr ""
"Ang code na ito ay karaniwang tinatawag na *ang 5-qubit code.*\n"
"Ito ang pinakamaliit na bilang ng mga qubit sa isang quantum error correcting code na maaaring magpahintulot ng pagwawasto ng isang arbitrary na single-qubit error.\n"

#. type: Title ###
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "One-dimensional stabilizer codes {#one-dimensional-stabilizer-codes}"
msgstr ""
"Mga one-dimensional na stabilizer code {#one-dimensional-stabilizer-codes}"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Here's another example of a stabilizer code, though it doesn't actually encode any qubits:\n"
"the code space is one-dimensional.\n"
"It is, however, still a valid stabilizer code by the definition.\n"
msgstr ""
"Narito ang isa pang halimbawa ng isang stabilizer code, kahit na hindi ito aktwal na nag-e-encode ng anumang qubit:\n"
"ang code space ay one-dimensional.\n"
"Gayunpaman, ito ay isang wastong stabilizer code pa rin ayon sa kahulugan.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"\\begin{array}{cc}\n"
"Z & Z \\\\[1mm]\n"
"X & X\n"
"\\end{array}\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"\\begin{array}{cc}\n"
"Z & Z \\\\[1mm]\n"
"X & X\n"
"\\end{array}\n"
"$$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Specifically, the code space is the one-dimensional space spanned by an "
"e-bit $\\vert\\phi^+\\rangle.$\n"
msgstr ""
"Sa partikular, ang code space ay ang one-dimensional na espasyo na "
"isinasaklaw ng isang e-bit na $\\vert\\phi^+\\rangle.$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Here's a related example of a stabilizer code whose code space is the one-"
"dimensional space spanned by a GHZ state $(\\vert 000\\rangle + \\vert "
"111\\rangle)/\\sqrt{2}.$\n"
msgstr ""
"Narito ang isang kaugnay na halimbawa ng isang stabilizer code na ang code "
"space ay ang one-dimensional na espasyo na isinasaklaw ng isang GHZ state na"
" $(\\vert 000\\rangle + \\vert 111\\rangle)/\\sqrt{2}.$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"\\begin{array}{cc}\n"
"Z & Z & \\mathbb{I} \\\\[1mm]\n"
"\\mathbb{I} & Z & Z \\\\[1mm]\n"
"X & X & X\n"
"\\end{array}\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"\\begin{array}{cc}\n"
"Z & Z & \\mathbb{I} \\\\[1mm]\n"
"\\mathbb{I} & Z & Z \\\\[1mm]\n"
"X & X & X\n"
"\\end{array}\n"
"$$\n"

#. type: Title ##
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Code space dimension {#code-space-dimension}"
msgstr "Dimensyon ng code space {#code-space-dimension}"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Suppose that we have a stabilizer code, described by $n$-qubit stabilizer generators $P_1,\\ldots,P_r.$\n"
"Perhaps the very first question that comes to mind about this code is, \"How many qubits does it encode?\"\n"
msgstr ""
"Ipagpalagay na mayroon tayong isang stabilizer code, na inilalarawan ng $n$-qubit na mga stabilizer generator na $P_1,\\ldots,P_r.$\n"
"Marahil ang pinaka-unang tanong na pumapasok sa isip tungkol sa code na ito ay, \"Ilang qubit ang ini-encode nito?\"\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"This question has a simple answer.\n"
"Assuming that the $n$-qubit stabilizer generators $P_1, \\ldots, P_r$ satisfy the three requirements of the definition (namely, that the stabilizer generators all commute with one another, that this is a minimal generating set, and that the code space is nonempty), it must then be that the code space for this stabilizer code has dimension $2^{n-r},$ so $n-r$ qubits can be encoded using this code.\n"
msgstr ""
"Ang tanong na ito ay may simpleng sagot.\n"
"Kung ipinapalagay na ang $n$-qubit na mga stabilizer generator na $P_1, \\ldots, P_r$ ay natutugunan ang tatlong kinakailangan ng kahulugan (ibig sabihin, ang lahat ng stabilizer generator ay nag-commute sa isa't isa, ito ay isang minimal generating set, at ang code space ay hindi walang laman), dapat na ang code space para sa stabilizer code na ito ay may dimensyong $2^{n-r},$ kaya ang $n-r$ na mga qubit ay maaaring ma-encode gamit ang code na ito.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Intuitively speaking, we have $n$ qubits to use for this encoding, and each stabilizer generator effectively \"takes a qubit away\" in terms of how many qubits we can encode.\n"
"Note that this is not about which or how many *errors* can be detected or corrected, it is only a statement about the dimension of the code space.\n"
msgstr ""
"Sa intuitive na pagsasalita, mayroon tayong $n$ na qubit upang gamitin para sa encoding na ito, at ang bawat stabilizer generator ay epektibong \"nag-aalis ng isang qubit\" sa mga tuntunin ng kung ilang qubit ang maaari nating i-encode.\n"
"Tandaan na hindi ito tungkol sa kung aling o gaano karaming mga *error* ang maaaring matuklas o maiwasto, ito ay isang pahayag lamang tungkol sa dimensyon ng code space.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"For example, for both the 3-bit repetition code and the modified version of that code for phase-flip errors, we have $n=3$ qubits and $r=2$ stabilizer generators, and therefore these codes can each encode 1 qubit.\n"
"For another example, consider the 5-qubit code: we have 5 qubits and 4 stabilizer generators, so once again the code space has dimension 2, meaning that one qubit can be encoded using this code.\n"
"For one final example, the code whose stabilizer generators are $X\\otimes X$ and $Z\\otimes Z$ has a one-dimensional code space, spanned by the state $\\vert\\phi^+\\rangle,$ which is consistent with having $n=2$ qubits and $r=2$ stabilizer generators.\n"
msgstr ""
"Halimbawa, para sa parehong 3-bit repetition code at ang binagong bersyon ng code na iyon para sa mga phase-flip error, mayroon tayong $n=3$ na qubit at $r=2$ na stabilizer generator, at samakatuwid ang mga code na ito ay bawat isa ay maaaring mag-encode ng 1 qubit.\n"
"Para sa isa pang halimbawa, isaalang-alang ang 5-qubit code: mayroon tayong 5 qubit at 4 na stabilizer generator, kaya muli ang code space ay may dimensyon 2, ibig sabihin, ang isang qubit ay maaaring ma-encode gamit ang code na ito.\n"
"Para sa isang huling halimbawa, ang code na ang mga stabilizer generator ay $X\\otimes X$ at $Z\\otimes Z$ ay may one-dimensional na code space, na isinasaklaw ng estado na $\\vert\\phi^+\\rangle,$ na naaayon sa pagkakaroon ng $n=2$ na qubit at $r=2$ na stabilizer generator.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Now let's see how this fact can be proved.\n"
"The first step is to observe that, because the stabilizer generators commute, and because every Pauli operation is its own inverse, every element in the stabilizer can be expressed as a product\n"
msgstr ""
"Ngayon tingnan natin kung paano mapapatunayan ang katotohanang ito.\n"
"Ang unang hakbang ay obserbahan na, dahil nag-commute ang mga stabilizer generator, at dahil ang bawat Pauli operation ay ang sariling inverse nito, ang bawat elemento sa stabilizer ay maaaring ipahayag bilang isang produkto\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"P_1^{a_1} \\cdots P_r^{a_r},\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"P_1^{a_1} \\cdots P_r^{a_r},\n"
"$$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"where $a_1,\\ldots,a_r\\in\\{0,1\\}.$\n"
"Equivalently, each element of the stabilizer is obtained by multiplying together some subset of the stabilizer generators.\n"
"Indeed, every stabilizer element can be expressed *uniquely* in this way, due to the condition that $\\{P_1,\\ldots,P_r\\}$ is a minimal generating set.\n"
msgstr ""
"kung saan ang $a_1,\\ldots,a_r\\in\\{0,1\\}.$\n"
"Katumbas nito, ang bawat elemento ng stabilizer ay nakuha sa pamamagitan ng pagpaparami ng ilang subset ng mga stabilizer generator.\n"
"Sa katunayan, ang bawat elemento ng stabilizer ay maaaring ipahayag nang *natatangi* sa ganitong paraan, dahil sa kondisyon na ang $\\{P_1,\\ldots,P_r\\}$ ay isang minimal generating set.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Next, define $\\Pi_k$ to be the projection onto the space of $+1$-eigenvectors of $P_k,$ for each $k\\in\\{1,\\ldots,r\\}.$\n"
"These projections can be obtained by averaging the corresponding Pauli operations with the identity operation as follows.\n"
msgstr ""
"Susunod, tukuyin ang $\\Pi_k$ bilang ang projection patungo sa espasyo ng mga $+1$-eigenvector ng $P_k,$ para sa bawat $k\\in\\{1,\\ldots,r\\}.$\n"
"Ang mga projection na ito ay maaaring makuha sa pamamagitan ng pag-average ng mga kaukulang Pauli operation kasama ang identity operation tulad ng sumusunod.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"\\Pi_k = \\frac{\\mathbb{I}^{\\otimes n} + P_k}{2}\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"\\Pi_k = \\frac{\\mathbb{I}^{\\otimes n} + P_k}{2}\n"
"$$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"The code space $\\mathcal{C}$ is the subspace of all vectors that are fixed "
"by all $r$ of the stabilizer generators $P_1,\\ldots,P_r,$ or equivalently, "
"all $r$ of the projections $\\Pi_1,\\ldots,\\Pi_r.$\n"
msgstr ""
"Ang code space na $\\mathcal{C}$ ay ang subspace ng lahat ng vector na "
"naayos ng lahat ng $r$ na stabilizer generator na $P_1,\\ldots,P_r,$ o "
"katumbas nito, lahat ng $r$ na projection na $\\Pi_1,\\ldots,\\Pi_r.$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Given that the stabilizer generators all commute with one another, the projections $\\Pi_1,\\ldots,\\Pi_r$ must also commute.\n"
"This allows us to use a fact from linear algebra, which is that the *product* of these projections is the projection onto the *intersection* of the subspaces corresponding to the individual projections.\n"
"That is to say, the product $\\Pi_1\\cdots\\Pi_r$ is the projection onto the code space $\\mathcal{C}.$\n"
msgstr ""
"Dahil ang lahat ng stabilizer generator ay nag-commute sa isa't isa, ang mga projection na $\\Pi_1,\\ldots,\\Pi_r$ ay dapat ding nag-commute.\n"
"Nagbibigay-daan ito sa atin na gumamit ng isang katotohanan mula sa linear algebra, na ang *produkto* ng mga projection na ito ay ang projection patungo sa *interseksyon* ng mga subspace na tumutugma sa mga indibidwal na projection.\n"
"Ibig sabihin, ang produkto na $\\Pi_1\\cdots\\Pi_r$ ay ang projection patungo sa code space na $\\mathcal{C}.$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"We can now expand out the product $\\Pi_1\\cdots\\Pi_r$ using the formulas "
"for these projections to obtain the following expression.\n"
msgstr ""
"Maaari na nating palawakin ang produkto na $\\Pi_1\\cdots\\Pi_r$ gamit ang "
"mga formula para sa mga projection na ito upang makuha ang sumusunod na "
"ekspresyon.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"\\Pi_1\\cdots\\Pi_r\n"
"= \\biggl(\\frac{\\mathbb{I}^{\\otimes n} + P_1}{2}\\biggr)\\cdots\\biggl(\\frac{\\mathbb{I}^{\\otimes n} + P_r}{2}\\biggr)\n"
"= \\frac{1}{2^r}\\sum_{a_1,\\ldots,a_r \\in \\{0,1\\}} P_1^{a_1}\\cdots P_r^{a_r}\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"\\Pi_1\\cdots\\Pi_r\n"
"= \\biggl(\\frac{\\mathbb{I}^{\\otimes n} + P_1}{2}\\biggr)\\cdots\\biggl(\\frac{\\mathbb{I}^{\\otimes n} + P_r}{2}\\biggr)\n"
"= \\frac{1}{2^r}\\sum_{a_1,\\ldots,a_r \\in \\{0,1\\}} P_1^{a_1}\\cdots P_r^{a_r}\n"
"$$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"In words, the projection onto the code space of a stabilizer code is equal, "
"as a matrix, to the *average* over all of the elements in the stabilizer of "
"that code.\n"
msgstr ""
"Sa madaling salita, ang projection patungo sa code space ng isang stabilizer"
" code ay katumbas, bilang isang matrix, sa *average* sa lahat ng mga "
"elemento sa stabilizer ng code na iyon.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Finally, we can compute the dimension of the code space by using the fact that the dimension of any subspace is equal to the trace of the projection onto that subspace.\n"
"Thus, the dimension of the code space $\\mathcal{C}$ is given by the following formula.\n"
msgstr ""
"Sa wakas, maaari nating kalkulahin ang dimensyon ng code space sa pamamagitan ng paggamit ng katotohanang ang dimensyon ng anumang subspace ay katumbas ng trace ng projection patungo sa subspace na iyon.\n"
"Kaya, ang dimensyon ng code space na $\\mathcal{C}$ ay ibinibigay ng sumusunod na formula.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"\\operatorname{dim}(\\mathcal{C}) =\n"
"\\operatorname{Tr}(\\Pi_1\\cdots\\Pi_r) =\n"
"\\frac{1}{2^r} \\sum_{a_1,\\ldots,a_r \\in \\{0,1\\}} \\operatorname{Tr}(P_1^{a_1}\\cdots P_r^{a_r})\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"\\operatorname{dim}(\\mathcal{C}) =\n"
"\\operatorname{Tr}(\\Pi_1\\cdots\\Pi_r) =\n"
"\\frac{1}{2^r} \\sum_{a_1,\\ldots,a_r \\in \\{0,1\\}} \\operatorname{Tr}(P_1^{a_1}\\cdots P_r^{a_r})\n"
"$$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"We can evaluate this expression by making use of a couple of basic facts.\n"
msgstr ""
"Maaari nating suriin ang ekspresyong ito sa pamamagitan ng paggamit ng ilang"
" pangunahing katotohanan.\n"

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "We have $P_1^0 \\cdots P_r^0 = \\mathbb{I}^{\\otimes n}$ and therefore\n"
msgstr ""
"Mayroon tayong $P_1^0 \\cdots P_r^0 = \\mathbb{I}^{\\otimes n}$ at "
"samakatuwid\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"  $$\n"
"  \\operatorname{Tr}(P_1^{0}\\cdots P_r^{0}) = 2^n.\n"
"  $$\n"
msgstr ""
"  $$\n"
"  \\operatorname{Tr}(P_1^{0}\\cdots P_r^{0}) = 2^n.\n"
"  $$\n"

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"For $(a_1,\\ldots,a_r) \\neq (0,\\ldots,0),$ the product $P_1^{a_1}\\cdots "
"P_r^{a_r}$ must be $\\pm 1$ times a Pauli operation — but we cannot obtain "
"$\\mathbb{I}^{\\otimes n}$ because this would contradict the minimality of "
"the set $\\{P_1,\\ldots,P_r\\},$ and we cannot obtain "
"$-\\mathbb{I}^{\\otimes n}$ because the third condition on the stabilizer "
"generators forbids it. Therefore, because the trace of every non-identity "
"Pauli operation is zero, we obtain\n"
msgstr ""
"Para sa $(a_1,\\ldots,a_r) \\neq (0,\\ldots,0),$ ang produkto na "
"$P_1^{a_1}\\cdots P_r^{a_r}$ ay dapat na $\\pm 1$ beses ng isang Pauli "
"operation — ngunit hindi tayo makakakuha ng $\\mathbb{I}^{\\otimes n}$ dahil"
" ito ay magsasalungat sa minimalidad ng set na $\\{P_1,\\ldots,P_r\\},$ at "
"hindi tayo makakakuha ng $-\\mathbb{I}^{\\otimes n}$ dahil ipinagbabawal ito"
" ng ikatlong kondisyon sa mga stabilizer generator. Samakatuwid, dahil ang "
"trace ng bawat non-identity na Pauli operation ay zero, nakukuha natin\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"  $$\n"
"  \\operatorname{Tr}(P_1^{a_1}\\cdots P_r^{a_r}) = 0.\n"
"  $$\n"
msgstr ""
"  $$\n"
"  \\operatorname{Tr}(P_1^{a_1}\\cdots P_r^{a_r}) = 0.\n"
"  $$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "The dimension of the code space is therefore $2^{n-r}$ as claimed:\n"
msgstr ""
"Ang dimensyon ng code space ay samakatuwid ay $2^{n-r}$ tulad ng sinabi:\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"\\begin{aligned}\n"
"\\operatorname{dim}(\\mathcal{C}) & =\n"
"\\frac{1}{2^r} \\sum_{a_1,\\ldots,a_r \\in \\{0,1\\}} \\operatorname{Tr}(P_1^{a_1}\\cdots P_r^{a_r}) \\\\\n"
"& = \\frac{1}{2^r} \\operatorname{Tr}(P_1^{0}\\cdots P_r^{0}) \\\\\n"
"& = 2^{n-r}.\n"
"\\end{aligned}\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"\\begin{aligned}\n"
"\\operatorname{dim}(\\mathcal{C}) & =\n"
"\\frac{1}{2^r} \\sum_{a_1,\\ldots,a_r \\in \\{0,1\\}} \\operatorname{Tr}(P_1^{a_1}\\cdots P_r^{a_r}) \\\\\n"
"& = \\frac{1}{2^r} \\operatorname{Tr}(P_1^{0}\\cdots P_r^{0}) \\\\\n"
"& = 2^{n-r}.\n"
"\\end{aligned}\n"
"$$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"As an aside, we can now see that the assumption that $-\\mathbb{I}^{\\otimes n}$ is not contained in the stabilizer implies that the code space must contain at least one quantum state vector.\n"
"This is because, as we've just verified, this assumption implies that the code space has dimension $2^{n-r},$ which cannot be zero.\n"
"The converse implication happens to be trivial: if $-\\mathbb{I}^{\\otimes n}$ is contained in the stabilizer, then the code space can't possibly contain any quantum state vectors, because no nonzero vectors are fixed by this operation.\n"
msgstr ""
"Bilang karagdagan, makikita natin ngayon na ang pagpapalagay na ang $-\\mathbb{I}^{\\otimes n}$ ay hindi nakapaloob sa stabilizer ay nagpapahiwatig na ang code space ay dapat maglaman ng hindi bababa sa isang quantum state vector.\n"
"Ito ay dahil, tulad ng napatunayan natin, ang pagpapalagay na ito ay nagpapahiwatig na ang code space ay may dimensyong $2^{n-r},$ na hindi maaaring maging zero.\n"
"Ang kabaligtaran na implikasyon ay nangyayaring magiging trivial: kung ang $-\\mathbb{I}^{\\otimes n}$ ay nakapaloob sa stabilizer, ang code space ay hindi maaaring maglaman ng anumang quantum state vector, dahil walang nonzero na vector ang naayos ng operation na ito.\n"

#. type: Title ##
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Clifford operations and encodings {#clifford-operations-and-encodings}"
msgstr ""
"Mga Clifford na Operasyon at Encoding {#clifford-operations-and-encodings}"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Next, we'll briefly discuss how qubits can be encoded using stabilizer "
"codes, but to do that we first need to introduce *Clifford operations*.\n"
msgstr ""
"Susunod, tatalakayin natin nang maikli kung paano naka-encode ang mga qubit "
"gamit ang mga stabilizer code, pero para magawa iyon, kailangan muna nating "
"ipakilala ang mga *Clifford na operasyon*.\n"

#. type: Title ###
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Clifford operations {#clifford-operations}"
msgstr "Mga Clifford na Operasyon {#clifford-operations}"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Clifford operations are unitary operations, on any number of qubits, that can be implemented by quantum circuits with a restricted set of gates:\n"
"- Hadamard gates\n"
"- $S$ gates\n"
"- CNOT gates\n"
msgstr ""
"Ang mga Clifford na operasyon ay mga unitary na operasyon, sa anumang bilang ng mga qubit, na maaaring ipatupad sa pamamagitan ng mga quantum circuit na gumagamit ng limitadong hanay ng mga Gate:\n"
"- Mga Hadamard gate\n"
"- Mga $S$ gate\n"
"- Mga CNOT gate\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Notice that $T$ gates are not included, nor are Toffoli gates and Fredkin gates.\n"
"Not only are those gates not included in the list, but in fact, it's not possible to implement those gates using the ones listed here; they're not Clifford operations.\n"
"Pauli operations, on the other hand, are Clifford operations because they can be implemented with sequences of Hadamard and $S$ gates.\n"
msgstr ""
"Pansinin na hindi kasama ang mga $T$ gate, ni ang mga Toffoli gate at Fredkin gate.\n"
"Hindi lamang hindi sila kasama sa listahan — sa katunayan, hindi posibleng ipatupad ang mga gate na iyon gamit ang mga nakalistang dito; hindi sila mga Clifford na operasyon.\n"
"Ang mga Pauli na operasyon naman ay mga Clifford na operasyon dahil maaari itong ipatupad gamit ang mga pagkakasunud-sunod ng Hadamard at $S$ gate.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"That's a simple way to define Clifford operations, but it doesn't explain why they're defined like this or what's special about this particular collection of gates.\n"
"The *real* reason Clifford operations are defined like this is that, up to global phase factors, the Clifford operations are precisely the unitary operations that always transform Pauli operations into Pauli operations by conjugation.\n"
"To be more precise, an $n$-qubit unitary operation $U$ is equivalent to a Clifford operation up to a phase factor if, and only if, for *every* $n$-qubit Pauli operation $P,$ we have\n"
msgstr ""
"Iyon ay isang simpleng paraan para tukuyin ang mga Clifford na operasyon, ngunit hindi nito ipinapaliwanag kung bakit ganito ang kanilang kahulugan o ano ang espesyal sa partikular na koleksyong ito ng mga gate.\n"
"Ang *tunay* na dahilan kung bakit ganito ang kahulugan ng mga Clifford na operasyon ay ang mga ito, hanggang sa mga pandaigdigang phase factor, ay tiyak na ang mga unitary na operasyon na palaging nagko-conjugate ng mga Pauli na operasyon at nagreresulta sa mga Pauli na operasyon.\n"
"Para maging mas tiyak, ang isang $n$-qubit na unitary na operasyon $U$ ay katumbas ng isang Clifford na operasyon hanggang sa isang phase factor kung, at kung lamang, para sa *bawat* $n$-qubit na Pauli na operasyon $P,$ mayroon tayong\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"U P U^{\\dagger} = \\pm Q\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"U P U^{\\dagger} = \\pm Q\n"
"$$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "for some $n$-qubit Pauli operation $Q.$\n"
msgstr "para sa ilang $n$-qubit na Pauli na operasyon $Q.$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"(Note that it is not possible to have $U P U^{\\dagger} = \\alpha Q$ for $\\alpha\\notin\\{+1,-1\\}$ when $U$ is unitary and $P$ and $Q$ are Pauli operations.\n"
"This follows from the fact that the matrix on the left-hand side of the equation in question is both unitary and Hermitian, and $+1$ and $-1$ are the only choices for $\\alpha$ that allow the right-hand side to be unitary and Hermitian as well.)\n"
msgstr ""
"(Pansinin na hindi posible na magkaroon ng $U P U^{\\dagger} = \\alpha Q$ para sa $\\alpha\\notin\\{+1,-1\\}$ kapag ang $U$ ay unitary at ang $P$ at $Q$ ay mga Pauli na operasyon.\n"
"Sumusunod ito mula sa katotohanang ang matrix sa kaliwang bahagi ng equation ay parehong unitary at Hermitian, at ang $+1$ at $-1$ ang tanging mga pagpipilian para sa $\\alpha$ na nagpapahintulot sa kanang bahagi na maging unitary at Hermitian din.)\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"It is straightforward to verify the conjugation property just described when $U$ is a Hadamard, $S,$ or CNOT gate.\n"
"In particular, this is easy for Hadamard gates,\n"
msgstr ""
"Madaling i-verify ang conjugation property na ito kapag ang $U$ ay isang Hadamard, $S,$ o CNOT gate.\n"
"Sa partikular, madali ito para sa mga Hadamard gate,\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"H X H^{\\dagger} = Z, \\qquad\n"
"H Y H^{\\dagger} = -Y, \\qquad\n"
"H Z H^{\\dagger} = X,\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"H X H^{\\dagger} = Z, \\qquad\n"
"H Y H^{\\dagger} = -Y, \\qquad\n"
"H Z H^{\\dagger} = X,\n"
"$$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "and $S$ gates,\n"
msgstr "at mga $S$ gate,\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"S X S^{\\dagger} = Y, \\qquad\n"
"S Y S^{\\dagger} = -X, \\qquad\n"
"S Z S^{\\dagger} = Z.\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"S X S^{\\dagger} = Y, \\qquad\n"
"S Y S^{\\dagger} = -X, \\qquad\n"
"S Z S^{\\dagger} = Z.\n"
"$$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"For CNOT gates, there are 15 non-identity Pauli operations on two qubits to check.\n"
"Naturally, they can be checked individually — but the relationships between CNOT gates and $X$ and $Z$ gates listed (in circuit form) in the previous lesson, together with the multiplication rules for Pauli matrices, offer a shortcut to the same conclusion.\n"
msgstr ""
"Para sa mga CNOT gate, may 15 na di-pagkakakilanlan na Pauli na operasyon sa dalawang qubit na kailangang suriin.\n"
"Natural, maaari silang suriin nang isa-isa — ngunit ang mga relasyon sa pagitan ng mga CNOT gate at mga $X$ at $Z$ gate na nakalista (sa anyo ng circuit) sa nakaraang aralin, kasama ang mga patakaran sa pagpaparami ng mga Pauli matrix, ay nag-aalok ng shortcut patungo sa parehong konklusyon.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Once we know this conjugation property is true for Hadamard, $S,$ and CNOT "
"gates, we can immediately conclude that it is true for *circuits* composed "
"of these gates — which is to say, all Clifford operations.\n"
msgstr ""
"Kapag nalaman na natin na ang conjugation property na ito ay totoo para sa "
"mga Hadamard, $S,$ at CNOT gate, maaari tayong agad na magsimulang tapusin "
"na ito ay totoo para sa mga *circuit* na binubuo ng mga gate na ito — ibig "
"sabihin, lahat ng Clifford na operasyon.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"It is more difficult to prove that the relationship works in the other direction, which is that if a given unitary operation $U$ satisfies the conjugation property for Pauli operations, then it must be possible to implement it (up to a global phase) using just Hadamard, $S,$ and CNOT gates.\n"
"This won't be explained in this lesson, but it is true.\n"
msgstr ""
"Mas mahirap patunayan na ang relasyon ay gumagana sa kabilang direksyon, na kung ang isang ibinigay na unitary na operasyon $U$ ay nakakatugon sa conjugation property para sa mga Pauli na operasyon, kailangang posibleng ipatupad ito (hanggang sa isang global phase) gamit lamang ang Hadamard, $S,$ at CNOT gate.\n"
"Hindi ito ipapaliwanag sa araling ito, ngunit totoo ito.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Clifford operations are not universal for quantum computation; unlike universal sets of quantum gates, approximating arbitrary unitary operations to any desired level of accuracy with Clifford operations is not possible.\n"
"Indeed, for a given value of $n,$ there are only *finitely* many $n$-qubit Clifford operations (up to phase factors).\n"
"Performing Clifford operations on standard basis states followed by standard basis measurements also can't allow us to perform computations that are outside of the reach of classical algorithms — because we can *efficiently simulate* computations of this form classically.\n"
"This fact is known as the *Gottesman-Knill theorem*.\n"
msgstr ""
"Ang mga Clifford na operasyon ay hindi universal para sa quantum computation; hindi tulad ng mga universal na hanay ng quantum gate, hindi posible ang pag-aapproximate ng mga arbitrary na unitary na operasyon sa anumang nais na antas ng katumpakan gamit ang mga Clifford na operasyon.\n"
"Sa katunayan, para sa isang ibinigay na halaga ng $n,$ may *limitadong* bilang lamang ng mga $n$-qubit na Clifford na operasyon (hanggang sa mga phase factor).\n"
"Ang pagsasagawa ng mga Clifford na operasyon sa mga standard basis state na sinusundan ng mga standard basis measurement ay hindi rin nagbibigay-daan sa atin na magsagawa ng mga computation na wala sa abot ng mga klasikal na algorithm — dahil maaari tayong *mahusay na mag-simulate* ng mga computation na ganito nang klasikal.\n"
"Ang katotohanang ito ay kilala bilang *Gottesman-Knill theorem*.\n"

#. type: Title ###
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Encoders for stabilizer codes {#encoders-for-stabilizer-codes}"
msgstr ""
"Mga Encoder para sa mga Stabilizer Code {#encoders-for-stabilizer-codes}"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"A stabilizer code defines a code space of a certain dimension, and we have the freedom to use that code space however we choose —\n"
"nothing forces us to encode qubits into this code space in a specific way.\n"
"It is always possible, however, to use a *Clifford operation* as an encoder, if we choose to do that.\n"
"To be more precise, for any stabilizer code that allows $m$ qubits to be encoded into $n$ qubits, there's an $n$-qubit Clifford operation $U$ such that, for any $m$-qubit quantum state vector $\\vert\\phi\\rangle,$ we have that\n"
msgstr ""
"Ang isang stabilizer code ay nagtatakda ng code space na may tiyak na dimensyon, at mayroon tayong kalayaang gamitin ang code space na iyon ayon sa ating kagustuhan —\n"
"walang pumipigil sa atin na i-encode ang mga qubit sa code space na ito sa isang tiyak na paraan.\n"
"Palagi itong posible, gayunpaman, na gumamit ng *Clifford na operasyon* bilang encoder, kung pipiliin nating gawin iyon.\n"
"Para maging mas tiyak, para sa anumang stabilizer code na nagbibigay-daan sa pag-encode ng $m$ na qubit sa $n$ na qubit, may isang $n$-qubit na Clifford na operasyon $U$ na, para sa anumang $m$-qubit na quantum state vector $\\vert\\phi\\rangle,$ mayroon tayong\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"\\vert\\psi\\rangle = U \\bigl(\\vert 0^{n-m} \\rangle \\otimes \\vert \\phi\\rangle\\bigr)\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"\\vert\\psi\\rangle = U \\bigl(\\vert 0^{n-m} \\rangle \\otimes \\vert \\phi\\rangle\\bigr)\n"
"$$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"is a quantum state vector in the code space of our code that we may "
"interpret as an encoding of $\\vert\\phi\\rangle.$\n"
msgstr ""
"na isang quantum state vector sa code space ng ating code na maaari nating "
"interpretahin bilang encoding ng $\\vert\\phi\\rangle.$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"This is good because Clifford operations are relatively simple, compared with arbitrary unitary operations, and there are ways to optimize their implementation using techniques similar to ones found in the proof of the Gottesman-Knill theorem.\n"
"As a result, circuits for encoding states using stabilizer codes never need to be too large.\n"
"In particular, it is always possible to perform an encoding for an $n$-qubit stabilizer code using a Clifford operation that requires $O(n^2/\\log(n))$ gates.\n"
"This is because *every* Clifford operation on $n$ qubits can be implemented by a circuit of this size.\n"
msgstr ""
"Ito ay maganda dahil ang mga Clifford na operasyon ay medyo simple, kumpara sa mga arbitrary na unitary na operasyon, at may mga paraan para i-optimize ang kanilang implementasyon gamit ang mga teknik na katulad ng mga makikita sa patunay ng Gottesman-Knill theorem.\n"
"Bilang resulta, ang mga circuit para sa pag-encode ng mga state gamit ang mga stabilizer code ay hindi kailangang maging masyadong malaki.\n"
"Sa partikular, palaging posible na magsagawa ng encoding para sa isang $n$-qubit na stabilizer code gamit ang isang Clifford na operasyon na nangangailangan ng $O(n^2/\\log(n))$ gate.\n"
"Ito ay dahil ang *bawat* Clifford na operasyon sa $n$ na qubit ay maaaring ipatupad ng isang circuit na may sukat na ito.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"For example, here's an encoder for the 7-qubit Steane code.\n"
"It is indeed a Clifford operation, and as it turns out, this one doesn't even need $S$ gates.\n"
msgstr ""
"Halimbawa, narito ang isang encoder para sa 7-qubit Steane code.\n"
"Ito ay talagang isang Clifford na operasyon, at gaya ng lumalabas, ang isa na ito ay hindi na kailangan pang ng mga $S$ gate.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"![Clifford encoder for the 7-qubit Steane "
"code](/learning/images/courses/foundations-of-quantum-error-"
"correction/stabilizer-formalism/Steane-encoder.svg)\n"
msgstr ""
"![Clifford encoder para sa 7-qubit Steane "
"code](/learning/images/courses/foundations-of-quantum-error-"
"correction/stabilizer-formalism/Steane-encoder.svg)\n"

#. type: Title ##
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Detecting errors {#detecting-errors}"
msgstr "Pagde-detect ng mga Error {#detecting-errors}"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"For an $n$-qubit stabilizer code described by stabilizer generators "
"$P_1,\\ldots, P_r,$ error detection works in the following way.\n"
msgstr ""
"Para sa isang $n$-qubit na stabilizer code na inilalarawan ng mga stabilizer"
" generator na $P_1,\\ldots, P_r,$ ang pag-detect ng error ay gumagana sa "
"sumusunod na paraan.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"To detect errors, all of the stabilizer generators are measured as observables.\n"
"There are $r$ stabilizer generators, and therefore $r$ measurement outcomes, each one being $+1$ or $-1$ (or a binary value if we choose to associate $0$ with $+1$ and $1$ with $-1,$ respectively).\n"
"We interpret the $r$ outcomes collectively, as a vector or string, as a *syndrome.*\n"
"The syndrome $(+1,\\ldots,+1)$ indicates that no error has been detected, while at least one $-1$ somewhere within the syndrome indicates an error has been detected.\n"
msgstr ""
"Para ma-detect ang mga error, lahat ng stabilizer generator ay sinusukat bilang mga observable.\n"
"Mayroon $r$ na stabilizer generator, at samakatuwid $r$ na kinalabasan ng pagsukat, bawat isa ay $+1$ o $-1$ (o isang binary na halaga kung pipiliin nating iugnay ang $0$ sa $+1$ at $1$ sa $-1,$ ayon sa pagkakasunud-sunod).\n"
"Itinuturing natin ang $r$ na kinalabasan nang magkasama, bilang isang vector o string, bilang isang *syndrome.*\n"
"Ang syndrome na $(+1,\\ldots,+1)$ ay nagpapahiwatig na walang nadetektang error, habang ang kahit isang $-1$ sa loob ng syndrome ay nagpapahiwatig na may nadetektang error.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Suppose, in particular, that $E$ is an $n$-qubit Pauli operation, representing a hypothetical error.\n"
"(We're only considering Pauli operations as errors, by the way, because the discretization of errors works the same way for arbitrary stabilizer codes as it does for the 9-qubit Shor code.)\n"
"There are three cases that determine whether or not $E$ is detected as an error.\n"
msgstr ""
"Ipagpalagay, sa partikular, na ang $E$ ay isang $n$-qubit na Pauli na operasyon, na kumakatawan sa isang hypothetical na error.\n"
"(Isinasaalang-alang lamang natin ang mga Pauli na operasyon bilang mga error, sa pamamagitan ng paraan, dahil ang discretization ng mga error ay gumagana sa parehong paraan para sa mga arbitrary na stabilizer code tulad ng para sa 9-qubit Shor code.)\n"
"May tatlong kaso na nagtatakda kung nadetektahan ang $E$ bilang isang error o hindi.\n"

#. type: Title ###
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Error detection cases {#error-detection-cases}"
msgstr "Mga Kaso sa Pag-detect ng Error {#error-detection-cases}"

#. type: Bullet: '1. '
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "The operation $E$ is proportional to an element in the stabilizer.\n"
msgstr "Ang operasyon $E$ ay proporsyonal sa isang elemento sa stabilizer.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"   $$\n"
"   E = \\pm Q \\; \\text{for some}\\; Q \\in \\langle P_1,\\ldots,P_r\\rangle\n"
"   $$\n"
msgstr ""
"   $$\n"
"   E = \\pm Q \\; \\text{para sa ilang}\\; Q \\in \\langle P_1,\\ldots,P_r\\rangle\n"
"   $$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"   In this case, $E$ must commute with every stabilizer generator, so we "
"obtain the syndrome $(+1,\\ldots,+1).$  This means that $E$ is not detected "
"as an error.\n"
msgstr ""
"   Sa kasong ito, ang $E$ ay kailangang mag-commute sa bawat stabilizer "
"generator, kaya makukuha natin ang syndrome na $(+1,\\ldots,+1).$  "
"Nangangahulugan ito na ang $E$ ay hindi nadetektahan bilang isang error.\n"

#. type: Bullet: '2. '
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"The operation $E$ is not proportional to an element in the stabilizer, but "
"it nevertheless commutes with every stabilizer generator.\n"
msgstr ""
"Ang operasyon $E$ ay hindi proporsyonal sa isang elemento sa stabilizer, "
"ngunit nagko-commute pa rin ito sa bawat stabilizer generator.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"   $$\n"
"   E\\neq \\pm Q\\; \\text{for} \\; Q \\in \\langle P_1,\\ldots,P_r\\rangle, \\;\\text{but}\\;\n"
"   E P_k = P_k E \\;\\text{for every}\\; k\\in\\{1,\\ldots,r\\}\n"
"   $$\n"
msgstr ""
"   $$\n"
"   E\\neq \\pm Q\\; \\text{para sa} \\; Q \\in \\langle P_1,\\ldots,P_r\\rangle, \\;\\text{ngunit}\\;\n"
"   E P_k = P_k E \\;\\text{para sa bawat}\\; k\\in\\{1,\\ldots,r\\}\n"
"   $$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"   This is an error that changes vectors in the code space in some "
"nontrivial way. But, because $E$ commutes with every stabilizer generator, "
"the syndrome is $(+1,\\ldots,+1),$ so $E$ goes undetected by the code.\n"
msgstr ""
"   Ito ay isang error na nagbabago ng mga vector sa code space sa ilang di-"
"trivial na paraan. Ngunit, dahil ang $E$ ay nagko-commute sa bawat "
"stabilizer generator, ang syndrome ay $(+1,\\ldots,+1),$ kaya ang $E$ ay "
"hindi nadetektahan ng code.\n"

#. type: Bullet: '3. '
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"The operation $E$ anti-commutes with at least one of the stabilizer "
"generators.\n"
msgstr ""
"Ang operasyon $E$ ay nag-anti-commute sa kahit isa sa mga stabilizer "
"generator.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"   $$\n"
"   P_k E = -E P_k \\; \\text{for at least one} \\; k\\in\\{1,\\ldots,r\\}\n"
"   $$\n"
msgstr ""
"   $$\n"
"   P_k E = -E P_k \\; \\text{para sa kahit isa} \\; k\\in\\{1,\\ldots,r\\}\n"
"   $$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"   The syndrome is different than $(+1,\\ldots,+1),$ so the error $E$ is "
"detected by the code.\n"
msgstr ""
"   Ang syndrome ay iba sa $(+1,\\ldots,+1),$ kaya ang error $E$ ay "
"nadetektahan ng code.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"In the first case, the error $E$ is not a concern because this operation "
"does nothing to vectors in the code space, except to possibly inject an "
"irrelevant global phase: $E \\ket{\\psi} = \\pm\\ket{\\psi}$ for every "
"encoded state $\\ket{\\psi}.$ In essence, this is not actually an error — "
"whatever nontrivial action $E$ may have happens outside of the code space — "
"so it's good that $E$ is not detected as an error, because nothing needs to "
"be done about it.\n"
msgstr ""
"Sa unang kaso, ang error $E$ ay hindi isang alalahanin dahil ang operasyong "
"ito ay walang ginagawa sa mga vector sa code space, maliban sa posibleng "
"mag-inject ng isang hindi-kaugnay na global phase: $E \\ket{\\psi} = "
"\\pm\\ket{\\psi}$ para sa bawat naka-encode na state na $\\ket{\\psi}.$ Sa "
"esensya, hindi ito tunay na isang error — anumang di-trivial na aksyon ng "
"$E$ ay nangyayari sa labas ng code space — kaya maganda na ang $E$ ay hindi "
"nadetektahan bilang isang error, dahil wala namang kailangang gawin tungkol "
"dito.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"The second case, intuitively speaking, is the bad case.\n"
"It's the *anti-commutation* of an error with a stabilizer generator that causes a $-1$ to appear somewhere in the syndrome, signaling an error, but that doesn't happen in this case.\n"
"So, we have an error $E$ that does change vectors in the code space in some nontrivial way, but it goes undetected by the code.\n"
"For example, for the 3-bit repetition code, the operation $E = X\\otimes X\\otimes X$ falls into this category.\n"
msgstr ""
"Ang ikalawang kaso, sa intuitive na pagsasalita, ay ang masamang kaso.\n"
"Ito ay ang *anti-commutation* ng isang error sa isang stabilizer generator na nagdudulot ng $-1$ na lumabas sa isang lugar sa syndrome, na nagpapahiwatig ng isang error, ngunit hindi iyon nangyayari sa kasong ito.\n"
"Kaya, mayroon tayong error $E$ na nagbabago ng mga vector sa code space sa ilang di-trivial na paraan, ngunit ito ay hindi nadetektahan ng code.\n"
"Halimbawa, para sa 3-bit repetition code, ang operasyon $E = X\\otimes X\\otimes X$ ay napapabilang sa kategoryang ito.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"The fact that such an error $E$ must change some vectors in the code space in a non-trivial way can be argued as follows.\n"
"By the assumption that $E$ commutes with $P_1,\\ldots,P_r$ but is not proportional to a stabilizer element, we can conclude that we would obtain a new, valid stabilizer code by including $E$ as a stabilizer generator along with $P_1,\\ldots,P_r.$\n"
"The code space for this new code, however, has only half the dimension of the original code space, from which we can conclude that the action of $E$ on the original code space cannot be proportional to the identity operation.\n"
msgstr ""
"Ang katotohanan na ang ganitong error na $E$ ay kailangang magbago ng ilang vector sa code space sa isang di-trivial na paraan ay maaaring ipangalandakan tulad nito.\n"
"Sa pamamagitan ng pagpapalagay na ang $E$ ay nagko-commute sa $P_1,\\ldots,P_r$ ngunit hindi proporsyonal sa isang stabilizer element, maaari tayong magsimulang tapusin na makakakuha tayo ng isang bago, valid na stabilizer code sa pamamagitan ng pagsasama ng $E$ bilang isang stabilizer generator kasama ang $P_1,\\ldots,P_r.$\n"
"Ang code space para sa bagong code na ito, gayunpaman, ay may kalahating dimensyon lamang ng orihinal na code space, mula sa kung saan maaari tayong magsimulang tapusin na ang aksyon ng $E$ sa orihinal na code space ay hindi maaaring proporsyonal sa identity na operasyon.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"For the last of the three cases, which is that the error $E$ anti-commutes with at least one stabilizer generator,\n"
"the syndrome has at least one $-1$ somewhere in it, which indicates that something is wrong.\n"
"As we have already discussed, the syndrome won't uniquely identify $E$ in general, so it's still necessary to choose a correction operation for each syndrome, which might or might not correct the error $E.$\n"
"We'll discuss this step shortly, in the last part of the lesson.\n"
msgstr ""
"Para sa huli sa tatlong kaso, na ang error $E$ ay nag-anti-commute sa kahit isa sa mga stabilizer generator,\n"
"ang syndrome ay may kahit isang $-1$ sa isang lugar dito, na nagpapahiwatig na may mali.\n"
"Tulad ng napag-usapan na natin, ang syndrome ay hindi natatanging nagtatukoy sa $E$ sa pangkalahatan, kaya kinakailangan pa ring pumili ng correction operation para sa bawat syndrome, na maaaring o hindi makakatama sa error $E.$\n"
"Tatalakayin natin ang hakbang na ito sa lalong madaling panahon, sa huling bahagi ng aralin.\n"

#. type: Title ###
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Distance of a stabilizer code {#distance-of-a-stabilizer-code}"
msgstr "Distansya ng isang Stabilizer Code {#distance-of-a-stabilizer-code}"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"As a point of terminology, when we refer to the *distance* of a stabilizer code, we mean the *minimum weight* of a Pauli operation $E$ that falls into the second category above — meaning that it changes the code space in some nontrivial way, but the code doesn't detect this.\n"
"When it is said that a stabilizer code is an $[[n,m,d]]$ stabilizer code, using double square brackets, this means the following:\n"
msgstr ""
"Bilang isang punto ng terminolohiya, kapag tinutukoy natin ang *distansya* ng isang stabilizer code, ang ibig sabihin natin ay ang *pinakamababang weight* ng isang Pauli na operasyon $E$ na napapabilang sa ikalawang kategorya sa itaas — ibig sabihin, nagbabago ito ng code space sa ilang di-trivial na paraan, ngunit hindi ito nadetektahan ng code.\n"
"Kapag sinasabing ang isang stabilizer code ay isang $[[n,m,d]]$ na stabilizer code, gamit ang double square brackets, nangangahulugan ito ng sumusunod:\n"

#. type: Bullet: '1. '
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Encodings are $n$ qubits in length,\n"
msgstr "Ang mga encoding ay may haba na $n$ na qubit,\n"

#. type: Bullet: '2. '
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "the code allows for the encoding $m$ qubits, and\n"
msgstr "pinapahintulutan ng code ang pag-encode ng $m$ na qubit, at\n"

#. type: Bullet: '3. '
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "the distance of the code is $d.$\n"
msgstr "ang distansya ng code ay $d.$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"As an example, let's consider the 7-qubit Steane code.\n"
"Here are the stabilizer generators for this code:\n"
msgstr ""
"Bilang halimbawa, isaalang-alang natin ang 7-qubit Steane code.\n"
"Narito ang mga stabilizer generator para sa code na ito:\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "This code has distance 3, and we can argue this as follows.\n"
msgstr ""
"Ang code na ito ay may distansyang 3, at maaari nating ipangalandakan ito "
"tulad nito.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"First consider any Pauli operation $E$ having weight at most 2, and suppose this operation commutes with all six stabilizer generators.\n"
"We will conclude that $E$ must be the identity operation, which (as always) is an element of the stabilizer.\n"
"This will show that the distance of the code is strictly greater than 2.\n"
"Suppose, in particular, that $E$ takes the form\n"
msgstr ""
"Una, isaalang-alang ang anumang Pauli na operasyon $E$ na may weight na hindi hihigit sa 2, at ipagpalagay na nagko-commute ang operasyong ito sa lahat ng anim na stabilizer generator.\n"
"Magsisimula tayong tapusin na ang $E$ ay kailangang maging identity na operasyon, na (tulad ng palagi) ay isang elemento ng stabilizer.\n"
"Ipapakita nito na ang distansya ng code ay higit sa 2 nang mahigpit.\n"
"Ipagpalagay, sa partikular, na ang $E$ ay may anyo\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"E = P \\otimes Q \\otimes \\mathbb{I} \\otimes \\mathbb{I} \\otimes \\mathbb{I} \\otimes \\mathbb{I} \\otimes \\mathbb{I}\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"E = P \\otimes Q \\otimes \\mathbb{I} \\otimes \\mathbb{I} \\otimes \\mathbb{I} \\otimes \\mathbb{I} \\otimes \\mathbb{I}\n"
"$$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"for $P$ and $Q$ being possibly non-identity Pauli matrices.\n"
"This is just one case, and it is necessary to repeat the argument that follows for all of the other possible locations for non-identity Pauli matrices among the tensor factors of $E,$ but the argument is essentially the same for all of the possible locations.\n"
msgstr ""
"para sa $P$ at $Q$ na posibleng di-identity na Pauli matrix.\n"
"Ito ay isang kaso lamang, at kinakailangang ulitin ang argumento na sumusunod para sa lahat ng iba pang posibleng lokasyon para sa mga di-identity na Pauli matrix sa mga tensor factor ng $E,$ ngunit ang argumento ay halos kapareho para sa lahat ng posibleng lokasyon.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"The operation $E$ commutes with all six stabilizer generators, so it "
"commutes with these two in particular:\n"
msgstr ""
"Ang operasyon $E$ ay nagko-commute sa lahat ng anim na stabilizer generator,"
" kaya nagko-commute ito sa dalawang ito sa partikular:\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"\\begin{gathered}\n"
"Z \\otimes \\mathbb{I} \\otimes Z \\otimes \\mathbb{I} \\otimes Z \\otimes \\mathbb{I} \\otimes Z\\\\[1mm]\n"
"X \\otimes \\mathbb{I} \\otimes X \\otimes \\mathbb{I} \\otimes X \\otimes \\mathbb{I} \\otimes X\n"
"\\end{gathered}\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"\\begin{gathered}\n"
"Z \\otimes \\mathbb{I} \\otimes Z \\otimes \\mathbb{I} \\otimes Z \\otimes \\mathbb{I} \\otimes Z\\\\[1mm]\n"
"X \\otimes \\mathbb{I} \\otimes X \\otimes \\mathbb{I} \\otimes X \\otimes \\mathbb{I} \\otimes X\n"
"\\end{gathered}\n"
"$$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"The tensor factor $Q$ in our error $E$ lines up with the identity matrix in both of these stabilizer generators (which is why they were selected).\n"
"Given that we have identity matrices in the rightmost 5 positions of $E,$ we conclude that $P$ must commute with $X$ and $Z,$ for otherwise $E$ would anti-commute with one of the two generators.\n"
"However, the only Pauli matrix that commutes with both $X$ and $Z$ is the identity matrix, so $P = \\mathbb{I}.$\n"
msgstr ""
"Ang tensor factor na $Q$ sa ating error na $E$ ay naka-linya sa identity matrix sa parehong stabilizer generator (kaya naman sila napili).\n"
"Dahil mayroon tayong mga identity matrix sa pinakakanan na 5 posisyon ng $E,$ magsisimula tayong tapusin na ang $P$ ay kailangang mag-commute sa $X$ at $Z,$ dahil kung hindi, ang $E$ ay mag-anti-commute sa isa sa dalawang generator.\n"
"Gayunpaman, ang tanging Pauli matrix na nagko-commute sa parehong $X$ at $Z$ ay ang identity matrix, kaya $P = \\mathbb{I}.$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Now that we know this, we can choose two more stabilizer generators that have an $X$ and a $Z$ in the second position from left, and we draw a similar conclusion: $Q = \\mathbb{I}.$\n"
"It is therefore the case that $E$ is the identity operation.\n"
msgstr ""
"Ngayon na alam na natin ito, maaari tayong pumili ng dalawa pang stabilizer generator na may $X$ at $Z$ sa ikalawang posisyon mula sa kaliwa, at makakakuha tayo ng katulad na konklusyon: $Q = \\mathbb{I}.$\n"
"Samakatuwid, ang $E$ ay ang identity na operasyon.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"So, there's no way for an error having weight at most 2 to go undetected by this code, unless the error is the identity operation (which is in the stabilizer and therefore not actually an error).\n"
"On the other hand, there are weight 3 Pauli operations that commute with all six of these stabilizer generators, but aren't proportional to stabilizer elements, such as $\\mathbb{I}\\otimes\\mathbb{I}\\otimes\\mathbb{I}\\otimes\\mathbb{I}\\otimes X\\otimes X\\otimes X$\n"
"and $\\mathbb{I}\\otimes\\mathbb{I}\\otimes\\mathbb{I}\\otimes\\mathbb{I}\\otimes Z\\otimes Z\\otimes Z.$\n"
"This establishes that this code has distance 3, as claimed.\n"
msgstr ""
"Kaya, walang paraan para ang isang error na may weight na hindi hihigit sa 2 ay hindi madetektahan ng code na ito, maliban kung ang error ay ang identity na operasyon (na nasa stabilizer at samakatuwid ay hindi tunay na isang error).\n"
"Sa kabilang banda, mayroon mga weight 3 na Pauli na operasyon na nagko-commute sa lahat ng anim na stabilizer generator na ito, ngunit hindi proporsyonal sa mga stabilizer element, tulad ng $\\mathbb{I}\\otimes\\mathbb{I}\\otimes\\mathbb{I}\\otimes\\mathbb{I}\\otimes X\\otimes X\\otimes X$\n"
"at $\\mathbb{I}\\otimes\\mathbb{I}\\otimes\\mathbb{I}\\otimes\\mathbb{I}\\otimes Z\\otimes Z\\otimes Z.$\n"
"Pinapatunayan nito na ang code na ito ay may distansyang 3, gaya ng sinabi.\n"

#. type: Title ##
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Correcting errors {#correcting-errors}"
msgstr "Pagwawasto ng mga Error {#correcting-errors}"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"The last topic of discussion for this lesson is the *correction* of errors for stabilizer codes.\n"
"As usual, assume that we have a stabilizer code specified by n-qubit stabilizer generators $P_1, \\ldots, P_r.$\n"
msgstr ""
"Ang huling paksa ng talakayan para sa araling ito ay ang *pagwawasto* ng mga error para sa mga stabilizer code.\n"
"Tulad ng dati, ipagpalagay na mayroon tayong stabilizer code na tinukoy ng n-qubit na stabilizer generator na $P_1, \\ldots, P_r.$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"The $n$-qubit Pauli operations, as errors that could affect states encoded using this code, are partitioned into equal-sized collections according to which syndrome they cause to appear.\n"
"There are $2^r$ distinct syndromes and $4^n$ Pauli operations, which means there are $4^n/2^r$ Pauli operations causing each syndrome.\n"
"Any one of these errors could be responsible for the corresponding syndrome.\n"
msgstr ""
"Ang mga $n$-qubit na Pauli na operasyon, bilang mga error na maaaring makaapekto sa mga state na naka-encode gamit ang code na ito, ay nahahati sa mga pantay na laking koleksyon ayon sa kung aling syndrome ang kanilang naisasanhi.\n"
"Mayroon $2^r$ na natatanging syndrome at $4^n$ na Pauli na operasyon, na nangangahulugang mayroon $4^n/2^r$ na Pauli na operasyon na nagsasanhi ng bawat syndrome.\n"
"Anuman sa mga error na ito ay maaaring responsable sa kaugnay na syndrome.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"However, among the $4^n/2^r$ Pauli operations that cause each syndrome, there are some that should be considered as being equivalent.\n"
"In particular, if the product of two Pauli operations is proportional to a stabilizer element, then those two operations are effectively equivalent as errors.\n"
msgstr ""
"Gayunpaman, sa gitna ng $4^n/2^r$ na Pauli na operasyon na nagsasanhi ng bawat syndrome, mayroon ilang dapat ituring na katumbas.\n"
"Sa partikular, kung ang produkto ng dalawang Pauli na operasyon ay proporsyonal sa isang stabilizer element, ang dalawang operasyong iyon ay epektibong katumbas bilang mga error.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Another way to say this is that if we apply a correction operation $C$ to attempt to correct an error $E,$ then this correction succeeds so long as the composition $CE$ is proportional to a stabilizer element.\n"
"Given that there are $2^r$ elements in the stabilizer, it follows that each correction operation $C$ corrects $2^r$ different Pauli errors.\n"
"This leaves $4^{n-r}$ inequivalent classes of Pauli operations, considered as errors, that are consistent with each possible syndrome.\n"
msgstr ""
"Isa pang paraan para sabihin ito ay kung maglalapat tayo ng correction operation na $C$ para subukang itama ang isang error na $E,$ ang pagwawasto na ito ay matagumpay hangga't ang komposisyon na $CE$ ay proporsyonal sa isang stabilizer element.\n"
"Dahil mayroon $2^r$ na elemento sa stabilizer, sumusunod na ang bawat correction operation na $C$ ay nagtutuwid ng $2^r$ na iba't ibang Pauli error.\n"
"Nag-iiwan ito ng $4^{n-r}$ na hindi magkaparehong klase ng Pauli na operasyon, itinuturing bilang mga error, na naaayon sa bawat posibleng syndrome.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"This means that, unless $n=r$ (in which case we have a trivial, one-dimensional code space), we can't possibly correct every error detected by a stabilizer code.\n"
"What we must do instead is to choose just *one* correction operation for each syndrome, in the hopes of correcting just one class of equivalent errors that cause this syndrome.\n"
msgstr ""
"Nangangahulugan ito na, maliban kung ang $n=r$ (kung saan mayroon tayong trivial, isang-dimensional na code space), hindi natin maaaring itama ang bawat error na nadetektahan ng isang stabilizer code.\n"
"Ang dapat nating gawin sa halip ay pumili ng *isang* correction operation para sa bawat syndrome, sa pag-asa na maitama ang isang klase lamang ng katumbas na mga error na nagsasanhi ng syndrome na ito.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"One natural strategy for choosing which correction operation to perform for each syndrome is to choose the *lowest weight* Pauli operation that, as an error, causes that syndrome.\n"
"There may in fact be multiple operations that tie for the lowest weight error consistent with a given syndrome, in which case any one of them may be selected.\n"
"The idea is that lower-weight Pauli operations represent more likely explanations for whatever syndrome has been measured.\n"
"This might actually not be the case for some noise models, and one alternative strategy is to compute the most *likely* error that causes the given syndrome, based on the chosen noise model.\n"
"For this lesson, however, we'll keep things simple and only consider lowest-weight corrections.\n"
msgstr ""
"Ang isang natural na estratehiya para pumili ng kung aling correction operation ang isasagawa para sa bawat syndrome ay ang pumili ng *pinakamababang weight* na Pauli na operasyon na, bilang isang error, ay nagsasanhi ng syndrome na iyon.\n"
"Maaaring mayroon sa katunayan ng maramihang operasyon na nagtatali para sa pinakamababang weight na error na naaayon sa isang ibinigay na syndrome, kung saan anuman sa mga ito ay maaaring mapili.\n"
"Ang ideya ay ang mga Pauli na operasyon na may mas mababang weight ay kumakatawan sa mas malamang na mga paliwanag para sa anumang syndrome na nasukat.\n"
"Maaaring hindi ito ang kaso para sa ilang noise model, at ang isang alternatibong estratehiya ay ang mag-compute ng pinaka-*malamang* na error na nagsasanhi ng ibinigay na syndrome, batay sa piniling noise model.\n"
"Para sa araling ito, gayunpaman, pinanatili nating simple ang mga bagay at isinasaalang-alang lamang ang mga pinakamababang weight na pagwawasto.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"For a distance $d$ stabilizer code, this strategy of choosing the correction operation to be a lowest weight Pauli operation consistent with the measured syndrome always allows for the correction of errors having weight strictly less than half of $d,$ or in other words, weight at most $(d-1)/2.$\n"
"This shows, for instance, that the 7-qubit Steane code can correct for any weight-one Pauli error, and by the discretization of errors, this means that the Steane code can correct for an arbitrary error on one qubit.\n"
msgstr ""
"Para sa isang distansya $d$ na stabilizer code, ang estratehiyang ito ng pagpili ng correction operation na maging isang pinakamababang weight na Pauli na operasyon na naaayon sa nasukat na syndrome ay palaging nagbibigay-daan sa pagwawasto ng mga error na may weight na mahigpit na wala sa kalahati ng $d,$ o sa ibang salita, weight na hindi hihigit sa $(d-1)/2.$\n"
"Ipinapakita nito, halimbawa, na ang 7-qubit Steane code ay makakaitama ng anumang weight-one na Pauli error, at sa pamamagitan ng discretization ng mga error, nangangahulugan ito na ang Steane code ay makakaitama ng isang arbitrary na error sa isang qubit.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"To see how this works, consider the diagram below.\n"
"The circle on the left represents all of the Pauli operations that result in the syndrome $(+1,\\ldots,+1),$ which is the syndrome that suggests that no errors have occurred and nothing is wrong.\n"
"Among these operations we have elements of the stabilizer (or operations that are *proportional* to elements of the stabilizer, to be more precise) and we also have non-trivial errors that change the code space in some way but aren't detected by the code.\n"
"By the definition of distance, every Pauli operation in this category must have weight at least $d,$ because $d$ is defined as the minimum weight of these operations.\n"
msgstr ""
"Para makita kung paano gumagana ito, isaalang-alang ang diagram sa ibaba.\n"
"Ang bilog sa kaliwa ay kumakatawan sa lahat ng Pauli na operasyon na nagresulta sa syndrome na $(+1,\\ldots,+1),$ na ang syndrome na nagmumungkahi na walang naganap na error at walang mali.\n"
"Sa gitna ng mga operasyong ito mayroon tayo mga elemento ng stabilizer (o mga operasyon na *proporsyonal* sa mga elemento ng stabilizer, para maging mas tiyak) at mayroon din tayong mga di-trivial na error na nagbabago ng code space sa ilang paraan ngunit hindi nadetektahan ng code.\n"
"Sa kahulugan ng distansya, ang bawat Pauli na operasyon sa kategoryang ito ay kailangang may weight na hindi bababa sa $d,$ dahil ang $d$ ay tinukoy bilang ang pinakamababang weight ng mga operasyong ito.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"The circle on the right represents the Pauli operations that result in a "
"different syndrome $s\\neq(+1,\\ldots,+1),$ including an error $E$ having "
"weight strictly less than $d/2$ that we will consider.\n"
msgstr ""
"Ang bilog sa kanan ay kumakatawan sa mga Pauli na operasyon na nagresulta sa"
" ibang syndrome na $s\\neq(+1,\\ldots,+1),$ kabilang ang isang error $E$ na "
"may weight na mahigpit na wala sa $d/2$ na ating isasaalang-alang.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"![Lowest-weight error correction "
"diagram](/learning/images/courses/foundations-of-quantum-error-"
"correction/stabilizer-formalism/lowest-weight-correction.svg)\n"
msgstr ""
"![Diagram ng pinakamababang-weight na pagwawasto ng "
"error](/learning/images/courses/foundations-of-quantum-error-"
"correction/stabilizer-formalism/lowest-weight-correction.svg)\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"The correction operation $C$ chosen for the syndrome $s$ is the lowest weight Pauli operation in the collection represented by the circle on the right in the diagram (or any one of them in case there's a tie).\n"
"So, it could be that $C = E,$ but not necessarily.\n"
"What we can say for certain, however, is that $C$ cannot have weight larger than the weight of $E,$ because $C$ has minimal weight among the operations in this collection — and therefore $C$ has weight strictly less than $d/2.$\n"
msgstr ""
"Ang correction operation na $C$ na pinili para sa syndrome na $s$ ay ang pinakamababang weight na Pauli na operasyon sa koleksyon na kinakatawan ng bilog sa kanan sa diagram (o anuman sa kanila kung may tali).\n"
"Kaya, maaaring ang $C = E,$ ngunit hindi kinakailangan.\n"
"Ang maaari nating sabihin nang may katiyakan, gayunpaman, ay ang $C$ ay hindi maaaring magkaroon ng weight na mas malaki kaysa sa weight ng $E,$ dahil ang $C$ ay may minimal na weight sa gitna ng mga operasyon sa koleksyong ito — at samakatuwid ang $C$ ay may weight na mahigpit na wala sa $d/2.$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Now consider what happens when the correction operation $C$ is applied to whatever state we obtained after the error $E$ takes place.\n"
"Assuming that the original encoding was $\\vert\\psi\\rangle,$ we're left with $CE\\vert\\psi\\rangle.$\n"
"Our goal will be to show that $CE$ is proportional to an element in the stabilizer, implying that the correction is successful and (up to a global phase) we're left with the original encoded state $\\vert\\psi\\rangle.$\n"
msgstr ""
"Ngayon isaalang-alang kung ano ang mangyayari kapag ang correction operation na $C$ ay inilapat sa anumang state na nakuha natin pagkatapos mangyari ang error na $E.$\n"
"Ipagpalagay na ang orihinal na encoding ay $\\vert\\psi\\rangle,$ naiwan tayong may $CE\\vert\\psi\\rangle.$\n"
"Ang ating layunin ay ipakita na ang $CE$ ay proporsyonal sa isang elemento sa stabilizer, na nagpapahiwatig na ang pagwawasto ay matagumpay at (hanggang sa isang global phase) naiwan tayo ng orihinal na naka-encode na state na $\\vert\\psi\\rangle.$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"First, because $E$ and $C$ cause the same syndrome, the composition $CE$ must commute with every stabilizer generator.\n"
"In particular, if $P_k$ is any one of the stabilizer generators, then we must have\n"
msgstr ""
"Una, dahil ang $E$ at $C$ ay nagsasanhi ng parehong syndrome, ang komposisyon na $CE$ ay kailangang mag-commute sa bawat stabilizer generator.\n"
"Sa partikular, kung ang $P_k$ ay anuman sa mga stabilizer generator, kailangan nating magkaroon ng\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"P_k E = \\alpha E P_k\n"
"\\quad\\text{and}\\quad\n"
"P_k C = \\alpha C P_k\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"P_k E = \\alpha E P_k\n"
"\\quad\\text{at}\\quad\n"
"P_k C = \\alpha C P_k\n"
"$$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"for the same value of $\\alpha\\in\\{+1,-1\\},$ because this is the $k$-th entry in the syndrome $s$ that both $C$ and $E$ generate.\n"
"Hence, we have\n"
msgstr ""
"para sa parehong halaga ng $\\alpha\\in\\{+1,-1\\},$ dahil ito ang $k$-th na entry sa syndrome na $s$ na parehong $C$ at $E$ ang nagge-generate.\n"
"Samakatuwid, mayroon tayong\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"P_k (CE) = \\alpha C P_k E = \\alpha^2 (CE) P_k = (CE) P_k,\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"P_k (CE) = \\alpha C P_k E = \\alpha^2 (CE) P_k = (CE) P_k,\n"
"$$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"so $P_k$ commutes with $CE.$\n"
"We've therefore shown that $CE$ belongs in the circle on the left in the diagram, because it generates the syndrome $(+1,\\ldots,+1).$\n"
msgstr ""
"kaya nagko-commute ang $P_k$ sa $CE.$\n"
"Pinatunayan natin samakatuwid na ang $CE$ ay napapabilang sa bilog sa kaliwa sa diagram, dahil nagge-generate ito ng syndrome na $(+1,\\ldots,+1).$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Second, the composition $CE$ must have weight at most the sum of the weights of $C$ and $E$ — which follows from a moment's thought about products of Pauli operations — and therefore the weight of $CE$ is strictly less than $d.$\n"
"This implies that $CE$ is proportional to an element in the stabilizer of our code, which is what we wanted to show.\n"
"By choosing our correction operations to be lowest-weight representatives of the set of errors that generate each syndrome, we're therefore guaranteed to correct any Pauli errors having weight less than half of the distance of the code.\n"
msgstr ""
"Pangalawa, ang komposisyon na $CE$ ay kailangang magkaroon ng weight na hindi hihigit sa kabuuan ng mga weight ng $C$ at $E$ — na sumusunod mula sa sandaling pag-iisip tungkol sa mga produkto ng Pauli na operasyon — at samakatuwid ang weight ng $CE$ ay mahigpit na wala sa $d.$\n"
"Nangangahulugan ito na ang $CE$ ay proporsyonal sa isang elemento sa stabilizer ng ating code, na siyang nais nating ipakita.\n"
"Sa pamamagitan ng pagpili ng ating mga correction operation na maging mga pinakamababang-weight na kinatawan ng hanay ng mga error na nagge-generate ng bawat syndrome, garantisado nating maitatama ang anumang Pauli error na may weight na wala sa kalahati ng distansya ng code.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"There is one problem, however.\n"
"For stabilizer codes in general, it's a computationally difficult problem to compute the lowest weight Pauli operation causing a given syndrome.\n"
"(Indeed, this is true even for classical codes, which in this context we can think of as stabilizer codes where we only have $\\mathbb{I}$ and $Z$ matrices appearing as tensor factors within the stabilizer generators.)\n"
"So, unlike the encoding step, Clifford operations will not be coming to our rescue this time.\n"
msgstr ""
"Mayroon, gayunpaman, isang problema.\n"
"Para sa mga stabilizer code sa pangkalahatan, ito ay isang computationally mahirap na problema ang mag-compute ng pinakamababang weight na Pauli na operasyon na nagsasanhi ng isang ibinigay na syndrome.\n"
"(Sa katunayan, totoo ito kahit para sa mga klasikal na code, na sa kontekstong ito ay maaari nating isipin bilang mga stabilizer code kung saan may $\\mathbb{I}$ at $Z$ lamang na matrix na lumalabas bilang mga tensor factor sa loob ng mga stabilizer generator.)\n"
"Kaya, hindi tulad ng encoding step, ang mga Clifford na operasyon ay hindi darating para iligtas tayo sa pagkakataong ito.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"The solution is to choose specific codes for which good corrections can be computed efficiently, for which there's no simple recipe.\n"
"Simply put, devising stabilizer codes for which good correction operations can be computed efficiently is part of the artistry of quantum code design.\n"
"We'll see this artistry on display in the next lesson.\n"
msgstr ""
"Ang solusyon ay pumili ng mga tiyak na code kung saan ang mga magagandang pagwawasto ay maaaring ma-compute nang mahusay, na walang simpleng recipe para dito.\n"
"Sa madaling salita, ang pagbuo ng mga stabilizer code kung saan ang mga magagandang correction operation ay maaaring ma-compute nang mahusay ay bahagi ng sining ng quantum code design.\n"
